INSERT INTO devotions (id, sort, reference, text, reflection, declaration, prayer) VALUES
 ('dy001', 1, 'Isaiah 43:18-19', 'Remember ye not the former things, neither consider the things of old. Behold, I will do a new thing; now it shall spring forth; shall ye not know it? I will even make a way in the wilderness, and rivers in the desert.', 'God is not asking you to carry last year into this one. He is already doing something new, and He can make a way where you see only wilderness.', 'I release the former things. God is doing a new thing in my life, and He is making a way for me in the wilderness.', 'Father, thank You for a fresh start. Help me to stop rehearsing the past and to see the new thing You are bringing forth. Make a way for me this year, and let rivers flow in my dry places. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy002', 2, 'Lamentations 3:22-23', 'It is of the LORD''s mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not. They are new every morning: great is thy faithfulness.', 'You woke up to new mercy this morning. Whatever yesterday held, God''s compassion has not run out, and His faithfulness is greater than your failures.', 'I am kept by the Lord''s mercies. His compassions do not fail me, they are new every morning, and great is His faithfulness to me.', 'Lord, thank You that Your mercy met me again this morning. When I feel tired or behind, remind me that Your compassion never fails. I rest in Your great faithfulness today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy003', 3, '2 Corinthians 5:17', 'Therefore if any man be in Christ, he is a new creature: old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new.', 'In Christ you are not just improved; you are made new. Your old labels and old record do not define who you are today.', 'I am in Christ, so I am a new creation. Old things have passed away, and all things have become new in me.', 'Jesus, thank You for making me new. Help me to live from who I am in You, not from who I used to be. Let the newness You have given me show in my thoughts, words, and choices today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy004', 4, 'Matthew 6:33', 'But seek ye first the kingdom of God, and his righteousness; and all these things shall be added unto you.', 'Before the plans, the goals, and the to-do list, put God first. As you seek His kingdom, He faithfully takes care of what you need.', 'I seek first the kingdom of God and His righteousness, and I trust my Father to add to me the things I need.', 'Father, I choose to put You first this year. Quiet my worries about what I need and turn my heart toward Your kingdom. I trust You to provide as I seek You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy005', 5, 'Habakkuk 2:2-3', 'And the LORD answered me, and said, Write the vision, and make it plain upon tables, that he may run that readeth it. For the vision is yet for an appointed time, but at the end it shall speak, and not lie: though it tarry, wait for it; because it will surely come, it will not tarry.', 'Write down what God has placed on your heart. His vision has an appointed time; even if it seems slow, keep waiting on Him.', 'I write the vision God gives me and make it plain. Though it tarries, I will wait for it, because at His appointed time it will speak.', 'Lord, give me clear vision for this year and help me write it plainly. Teach me patience when things seem delayed, and keep me trusting Your timing. Let what You have spoken come to pass. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy006', 6, 'Psalm 32:8', 'I will instruct thee and teach thee in the way which thou shalt go: I will guide thee with mine eye.', 'You do not have to figure out every step alone. God promises to instruct you, teach you, and guide you with His loving attention.', 'The Lord instructs me and teaches me in the way I should go. He guides me with His eye upon me.', 'Father, I invite You to teach me the way I should go today. Keep Your eye upon me and guide my decisions. Make me sensitive and willing to follow Your leading. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy007', 7, 'Isaiah 30:21', 'And thine ears shall hear a word behind thee, saying, This is the way, walk ye in it, when ye turn to the right hand, and when ye turn to the left.', 'When you stand at a crossroads, listen. God speaks to His people and gently points out the way to walk.', 'My ears will hear God''s word behind me saying, This is the way, walk in it. I will not be lost at the crossroads.', 'Lord, tune my ears to Your voice. When I turn to the right or to the left, speak and show me the way. Give me courage to walk in it. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy008', 8, 'Proverbs 16:3', 'Commit thy works unto the LORD, and thy thoughts shall be established.', 'Hand your work and plans to God. When you commit them to Him, He brings steadiness and order to your thinking.', 'I commit my works to the Lord, and my thoughts are established. My plans rest in His hands.', 'Father, I commit my work and my plans for this season to You. Settle my scattered thoughts and establish my mind. Let what I do honour You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy009', 9, 'Philippians 3:13-14', 'Brethren, I count not myself to have apprehended: but this one thing I do, forgetting those things which are behind, and reaching forth unto those things which are before, I press toward the mark for the prize of the high calling of God in Christ Jesus.', 'Paul did not claim to have arrived; he simply kept moving forward. Let go of what is behind and keep pressing toward God''s calling.', 'This one thing I do: I forget what is behind, I reach for what is ahead, and I press toward the prize of God''s high calling in Christ.', 'Lord Jesus, help me let go of what is behind me, both the failures and the old glories. Give me strength to keep reaching forward and pressing toward Your calling. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy010', 10, 'Psalm 90:12', 'So teach us to number our days, that we may apply our hearts unto wisdom.', 'Every day is a gift worth noticing. Ask God to help you treat your days with care so your heart grows in wisdom.', 'I will number my days and treat them as precious. I apply my heart to wisdom this year.', 'Lord, teach me to number my days. Help me not to waste the time You have given me, and turn my heart toward wisdom in the choices I make today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy011', 11, 'Hebrews 11:1', 'Now faith is the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen.', 'Faith is real even before the answer is visible. It is confident trust in God for what you hope for but cannot yet see.', 'My faith is the substance of things I hope for and the evidence of things not yet seen. I trust God beyond what my eyes can see.', 'Father, strengthen my faith this year. When I cannot see the outcome, help me trust You anyway. Let my hope rest firmly in who You are. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy012', 12, 'Psalm 37:4-5', 'Delight thyself also in the LORD: and he shall give thee the desires of thine heart. Commit thy way unto the LORD; trust also in him; and he shall bring it to pass.', 'As you delight in God, your desires begin to align with His heart. Commit your way to Him and trust Him to bring it to pass.', 'I delight myself in the Lord. I commit my way to Him and trust Him, and He will bring it to pass.', 'Lord, be my delight above everything else. I commit my way to You and choose to trust You. Shape the desires of my heart and bring to pass what You have planned. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy013', 13, 'Psalm 5:3', 'My voice shalt thou hear in the morning, O LORD; in the morning will I direct my prayer unto thee, and will look up.', 'Start your day by bringing your voice to God. Pray, then look up with expectation, because He hears you.', 'In the morning the Lord hears my voice. I direct my prayer to Him, and I look up with expectation.', 'Father, thank You for hearing me this morning. I lay my day before You and look up to You with hope. Guide every hour that follows. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy014', 14, 'Ezekiel 36:26', 'A new heart also will I give you, and a new spirit will I put within you: and I will take away the stony heart out of your flesh, and I will give you an heart of flesh.', 'God does not just ask you to try harder; He offers a new heart. He can soften what life has made hard in you.', 'God gives me a new heart and puts a new spirit within me. He takes away the stony heart and gives me a heart that is soft toward Him.', 'Lord, where my heart has grown hard or tired, make it new. Put Your Spirit within me and give me a tender heart toward You and others. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy015', 15, 'Psalm 119:105', 'Thy word is a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path.', 'God''s Word may not light up the whole road at once, but it gives enough light for your next step.', 'God''s Word is a lamp to my feet and a light to my path. I will not walk in darkness.', 'Father, thank You for Your Word. Light my next step today and keep me close to Scripture. When the way seems dark, let Your Word shine on my path. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy016', 16, 'Isaiah 58:11', 'And the LORD shall guide thee continually, and satisfy thy soul in drought, and make fat thy bones: and thou shalt be like a watered garden, and like a spring of water, whose waters fail not.', 'Even in a dry season, God can keep you fresh. He guides continually and makes your life like a watered garden that does not run dry.', 'The Lord guides me continually and satisfies my soul in drought. I am like a watered garden and a spring whose waters fail not.', 'Lord, guide me continually this year. In dry seasons, satisfy my soul and strengthen me. Make my life a watered garden that refreshes others. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy017', 17, 'James 1:5', 'If any of you lack wisdom, let him ask of God, that giveth to all men liberally, and upbraideth not; and it shall be given him.', 'You are allowed to ask God for wisdom without feeling foolish. He gives generously and does not scold you for asking.', 'When I lack wisdom, I ask God, who gives to me generously without reproach, and wisdom is given to me.', 'Father, I need Your wisdom for the decisions in front of me. Thank You that You give liberally and never scold me for asking. Fill me with wisdom today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy018', 18, 'Psalm 16:11', 'Thou wilt shew me the path of life: in thy presence is fulness of joy; at thy right hand there are pleasures for evermore.', 'God does not only show you where to go; He is the joy along the way. Real fullness of joy is found in His presence.', 'God shows me the path of life. In His presence I find fullness of joy, and at His right hand are pleasures forevermore.', 'Lord, show me the path of life. Draw me into Your presence, where my joy is made full. Let me find my deepest delight in You today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy019', 19, 'Matthew 7:7', 'Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you:', 'Jesus invites you to keep coming to God: asking, seeking, and knocking. Prayer is not a bother to Him; it is a welcome.', 'I ask, and it is given to me. I seek, and I find. I knock, and the door is opened to me.', 'Father, thank You for inviting me to ask, seek, and knock. Give me persistence in prayer and confidence that You hear me. Open the doors that are Yours for me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy020', 20, 'Psalm 27:4', 'One thing have I desired of the LORD, that will I seek after; that I may dwell in the house of the LORD all the days of my life, to behold the beauty of the LORD, and to enquire in his temple.', 'Among all the things you want this year, let one desire rise above them: to be near God and to behold His beauty.', 'One thing I desire of the Lord and will seek after: to dwell in His house all my days and to behold His beauty.', 'Lord, make You my one desire. Let me live close to You all the days of my life and see Your beauty more clearly. Teach me as I seek You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy021', 21, 'Isaiah 42:16', 'And I will bring the blind by a way that they knew not; I will lead them in paths that they have not known: I will make darkness light before them, and crooked things straight. These things will I do unto them, and not forsake them.', 'When the road ahead is unfamiliar, God knows it well. He leads, turns darkness into light, and promises not to abandon you.', 'God leads me in paths I have not known. He makes darkness light before me and crooked things straight, and He does not forsake me.', 'Father, I do not know every path ahead, but You do. Lead me, turn my darkness into light, and straighten what is crooked. Thank You for never forsaking me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy022', 22, 'Psalm 143:8', 'Cause me to hear thy lovingkindness in the morning; for in thee do I trust: cause me to know the way wherein I should walk; for I lift up my soul unto thee.', 'Let God''s love be the first thing you hear today. As you lift your soul to Him, ask Him to show you the way to walk.', 'In the morning I hear God''s lovingkindness, for in Him I trust. He causes me to know the way I should walk.', 'Lord, let me hear Your lovingkindness this morning. I put my trust in You and lift up my soul to You. Show me the way I should walk today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy023', 23, 'Deuteronomy 31:8', 'And the LORD, he it is that doth go before thee; he will be with thee, he will not fail thee, neither forsake thee: fear not, neither be dismayed.', 'Wherever you are heading, God has already gone ahead. He walks with you and will not let you go.', 'The Lord goes before me and is with me. He will not fail me or forsake me, so I will not fear or be dismayed.', 'Father, thank You for going before me into this year. Be with me in every place I step. Take away my fear and fill me with courage. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy024', 24, 'Proverbs 4:18', 'But the path of the just is as the shining light, that shineth more and more unto the perfect day.', 'Growth with God is often gradual, like the sunrise. Your path can grow brighter and brighter as you walk with Him.', 'My path is like the shining light, shining more and more unto the perfect day. My walk with God grows brighter.', 'Lord, let my path shine brighter as I walk with You. When growth feels slow, remind me that the dawn is still rising. Lead me toward the perfect day. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy025', 25, 'Isaiah 26:3', 'Thou wilt keep him in perfect peace, whose mind is stayed on thee: because he trusteth in thee.', 'Peace grows where your mind rests on God. When thoughts race, gently bring them back to Him and trust Him.', 'My mind is stayed on the Lord and I trust in Him, so He keeps me in perfect peace.', 'Father, when my mind is restless, draw my thoughts back to You. I choose to trust You. Keep me in Your perfect peace today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy026', 26, 'Micah 7:8', 'Rejoice not against me, O mine enemy: when I fall, I shall arise; when I sit in darkness, the LORD shall be a light unto me.', 'A fall is not the end of your story. With God, you can rise again, and even in darkness He is your light.', 'When I fall, I shall arise. When I sit in darkness, the Lord is a light to me.', 'Lord, thank You that falling is not final with You. Lift me up where I have stumbled and be my light in dark places. Help me start again with hope. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy027', 27, 'Psalm 63:1', 'O God, thou art my God; early will I seek thee: my soul thirsteth for thee, my flesh longeth for thee in a dry and thirsty land, where no water is;', 'That inner thirst you feel is ultimately for God. Seek Him early, and let Him meet you in your dry places.', 'O God, You are my God. Early will I seek You. My soul thirsts for You, even in a dry and thirsty land.', 'God, You are my God. I seek You early today. My soul is thirsty for You; meet me and refresh me in every dry place. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy028', 28, 'Psalm 118:24', 'This is the day which the LORD hath made; we will rejoice and be glad in it.', 'Today is not an accident; the Lord made it. Choose to find something in it to be glad about.', 'This is the day the Lord has made. I will rejoice and be glad in it.', 'Father, thank You for this day You have made. Open my eyes to Your goodness in it and fill my heart with gladness. Let my joy honour You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy029', 29, 'Hebrews 11:6', 'But without faith it is impossible to please him: for he that cometh to God must believe that he is, and that he is a rewarder of them that diligently seek him.', 'Faith pleases God. Come to Him believing that He is real and that He rewards those who diligently seek Him.', 'I come to God believing that He is, and that He rewards those who diligently seek Him. I will seek Him with my whole heart.', 'Father, I believe that You are, and that You reward those who seek You. Increase my faith and make me diligent in seeking You this year. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy030', 30, 'Psalm 25:4-5', 'Shew me thy ways, O LORD; teach me thy paths. Lead me in thy truth, and teach me: for thou art the God of my salvation; on thee do I wait all the day.', 'It is a good prayer to ask God to teach you. He is patient with learners and faithful to those who wait on Him.', 'The Lord shows me His ways and teaches me His paths. He leads me in His truth, and on Him I wait all the day.', 'Lord, show me Your ways and teach me Your paths. Lead me in Your truth, for You are the God of my salvation. I wait on You all day long. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy031', 31, 'Psalm 37:23-24', 'The steps of a good man are ordered by the LORD: and he delighteth in his way. Though he fall, he shall not be utterly cast down: for the LORD upholdeth him with his hand.', 'God cares about your steps, not just your destination. Even if you stumble, you will not be thrown down, because He holds your hand.', 'My steps are ordered by the Lord. Though I fall, I shall not be utterly cast down, for the Lord upholds me with His hand.', 'Father, order my steps as this month closes and a new one begins. When I stumble, hold me up with Your hand. Thank You for delighting in my way with You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy032', 32, '1 John 3:1', 'Behold, what manner of love the Father hath bestowed upon us, that we should be called the sons of God: therefore the world knoweth us not, because it knew him not.', 'Pause and look at this love: God calls you His child. That is not a title you earned; it is love He freely gave.', 'The Father has bestowed His love on me, and I am called a child of God.', 'Father, thank You for the love that makes me Your child. When I feel unseen or misunderstood, remind me whose I am. Let me live today as one who is deeply loved. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy033', 33, 'Jeremiah 31:3', 'The LORD hath appeared of old unto me, saying, Yea, I have loved thee with an everlasting love: therefore with lovingkindness have I drawn thee.', 'God''s love for you did not begin when you got things right, and it will not end when you get things wrong. It is everlasting.', 'The Lord has loved me with an everlasting love. With lovingkindness He has drawn me to Himself.', 'Lord, thank You for loving me with an everlasting love. Keep drawing me closer with Your lovingkindness. Let that love settle every fear in my heart today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy034', 34, 'Romans 5:8', 'But God commendeth his love toward us, in that, while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us.', 'God did not wait for you to become good enough. Christ died for you while you were still a sinner; that is how deep His love goes.', 'God has shown His love toward me: while I was still a sinner, Christ died for me. I am loved at my worst.', 'Father, thank You for loving me before I ever turned to You. Thank You, Jesus, for dying for me. Help me rest in that love and share it freely. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy035', 35, 'Zephaniah 3:17', 'The LORD thy God in the midst of thee is mighty; he will save, he will rejoice over thee with joy; he will rest in his love, he will joy over thee with singing.', 'Picture God rejoicing over you with singing. He is not just putting up with you; He is mighty to save and delights in you.', 'The Lord my God is in my midst and He is mighty. He saves me, rejoices over me with joy, and sings over me.', 'Mighty God, thank You for being in my midst. Help me to hear Your song over me today and to rest in Your love. Let Your joy over me become my strength. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy036', 36, 'Isaiah 49:15-16', 'Can a woman forget her sucking child, that she should not have compassion on the son of her womb? yea, they may forget, yet will I not forget thee. Behold, I have graven thee upon the palms of my hands; thy walls are continually before me.', 'Even the closest human love can fail, but God says He will never forget you. Your name is engraved on the palms of His hands.', 'God will not forget me. He has engraved me on the palms of His hands, and I am always before Him.', 'Lord, when I feel forgotten, remind me that I am engraved on Your hands. Thank You that Your love is more faithful than any other. Keep me ever before You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy037', 37, 'Romans 8:38-39', 'For I am persuaded, that neither death, nor life, nor angels, nor principalities, nor powers, nor things present, nor things to come, Nor height, nor depth, nor any other creature, shall be able to separate us from the love of God, which is in Christ Jesus our Lord.', 'Nothing in life or death, now or in the future, can cut you off from God''s love in Christ Jesus. You are held.', 'I am persuaded that nothing, not death nor life, nor things present nor things to come, can separate me from the love of God in Christ Jesus.', 'Father, thank You that nothing can separate me from Your love in Christ. Settle this truth deep in my heart. Let me face today unafraid, knowing I am held. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy038', 38, 'Ephesians 3:18-19', 'May be able to comprehend with all saints what is the breadth, and length, and depth, and height; And to know the love of Christ, which passeth knowledge, that ye might be filled with all the fulness of God.', 'Christ''s love is wider, longer, deeper, and higher than you can measure. Ask God to help you know it, not just know about it.', 'I am learning the breadth, length, depth, and height of the love of Christ, which passes knowledge, and I am filled with the fulness of God.', 'Lord, help me grasp how wide and deep Your love really is. Let me know the love of Christ beyond understanding, and fill me with all Your fulness. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy039', 39, '1 John 4:7', 'Beloved, let us love one another: for love is of God; and every one that loveth is born of God, and knoweth God.', 'Love comes from God. Every time you choose to love someone, you reflect the One who first loved you.', 'I love others, because love is of God. I am born of God and I know God.', 'Father, You are the source of all love. Fill me so full of Your love that it flows to the people around me today. Let my love show that I know You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy040', 40, 'John 15:12-13', 'This is my commandment, That ye love one another, as I have loved you. Greater love hath no man than this, that a man lay down his life for his friends.', 'Jesus sets the standard for love: love one another as He loved us. His self-giving love shows us what real friendship looks like.', 'I love others as Jesus has loved me. I am His friend, and I learn from His great, self-giving love.', 'Jesus, thank You for laying down Your life for me. Teach me to love others the way You have loved me, with patience and sacrifice. Make me a true friend. In Jesus'' name, Amen.');
INSERT INTO devotions (id, sort, reference, text, reflection, declaration, prayer) VALUES
 ('dy041', 41, '1 Corinthians 13:4-5', 'Charity suffereth long, and is kind; charity envieth not; charity vaunteth not itself, is not puffed up, Doth not behave itself unseemly, seeketh not her own, is not easily provoked, thinketh no evil;', 'Love is patient and kind. It does not show off, insist on its own way, or keep a list of wrongs. Ask God to grow this love in you.', 'With God''s help, my love suffers long and is kind. It does not envy, boast, or seek its own, and it is not easily provoked.', 'Lord, grow this kind of love in me. Make me patient where I am quick, kind where I am harsh, and humble where I am proud. Let my love look like Yours. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy042', 42, '1 Corinthians 13:7', 'Beareth all things, believeth all things, hopeth all things, endureth all things.', 'Real love does not give up easily. It carries weight, believes the best, keeps hoping, and holds on through hard seasons.', 'My love bears all things, believes all things, hopes all things, and endures all things, by the grace of God.', 'Father, give me love that endures. When relationships are hard, help me keep believing and hoping. Strengthen me to love the way You love me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy043', 43, 'Romans 12:10', 'Be kindly affectioned one to another with brotherly love; in honour preferring one another;', 'Treat the people around you like family. Look for ways to honour them and put them ahead of yourself.', 'I am kindly affectioned to others with brotherly love, and I choose to honour others above myself.', 'Lord, give me warm affection for the people You have placed around me. Show me how to honour them in words and actions today. Free me from needing to be first. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy044', 44, 'Proverbs 17:17', 'A friend loveth at all times, and a brother is born for adversity.', 'A true friend loves in every season, and family members are there for the hard times. Be that kind of friend today.', 'I am a friend who loves at all times. When adversity comes, I will stand by the people I love.', 'Father, thank You for the friends and family You have given me. Make me faithful in every season, especially when someone is struggling. Help me love at all times. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy045', 45, 'Proverbs 18:24', 'A man that hath friends must shew himself friendly: and there is a friend that sticketh closer than a brother.', 'Friendship grows when you show yourself friendly. And in Jesus you have a Friend who sticks closer than a brother.', 'I show myself friendly, and I have a Friend who sticks closer than a brother.', 'Jesus, thank You for being the Friend who sticks closer than a brother. Help me to reach out and be friendly to others. Lead me into healthy, godly friendships. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy046', 46, 'Ecclesiastes 4:9-10', 'Two are better than one; because they have a good reward for their labour. For if they fall, the one will lift up his fellow: but woe to him that is alone when he falleth; for he hath not another to help him up.', 'You were not made to do life alone. Two are better than one, because when one falls, the other can help them up.', 'Two are better than one. I will lift up others when they fall, and I receive help when I need it.', 'Lord, thank You for the people who walk with me. Help me be someone who lifts others up, and give me humility to accept help. Keep me from isolation. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy047', 47, 'Ruth 1:16', 'And Ruth said, Intreat me not to leave thee, or to return from following after thee: for whither thou goest, I will go; and where thou lodgest, I will lodge: thy people shall be my people, and thy God my God:', 'Ruth''s loyalty to Naomi is a beautiful picture of committed love. She chose to stay, and she chose Naomi''s God as her own.', 'Like Ruth, I choose loyal love. I stay close to those God has given me, and their God is my God.', 'Father, make me loyal and faithful in my relationships. Thank You for Ruth''s example of committed love. Help me stay close to the people You have given me and to You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy048', 48, 'Psalm 68:6', 'God setteth the solitary in families: he bringeth out those which are bound with chains: but the rebellious dwell in a dry land.', 'If you feel alone, God sees you. He places the lonely in families and brings people out of what binds them.', 'God sets the solitary in families. He places me among people who belong to me, and He brings me out of chains.', 'Lord, You see the lonely and You set them in families. Surround me with loving community and help me welcome others into it too. Break anything that holds me bound. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy049', 49, 'Psalm 133:1', 'Behold, how good and how pleasant it is for brethren to dwell together in unity!', 'There is something good and pleasant about God''s people living in unity. Choose peace and togetherness wherever you can today.', 'I value unity. It is good and pleasant for brethren to dwell together, and I will be a peacemaker in my home and church.', 'Father, bring unity to my family, my friendships, and my church. Make me a peacemaker, quick to build bridges. Let us dwell together in Your love. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy050', 50, 'Ephesians 4:32', 'And be ye kind one to another, tenderhearted, forgiving one another, even as God for Christ''s sake hath forgiven you.', 'Kindness and forgiveness flow from remembering how kindly God forgave you. Let His grace soften the way you treat others.', 'I am kind and tenderhearted toward others. I forgive, even as God for Christ''s sake has forgiven me.', 'Lord, thank You for forgiving me so fully. Make my heart tender and my words kind today. Help me forgive others as You have forgiven me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy051', 51, 'Micah 6:8', 'He hath shewed thee, O man, what is good; and what doth the LORD require of thee, but to do justly, and to love mercy, and to walk humbly with thy God?', 'God has made clear what is good: do what is right, love mercy, and walk humbly with Him. It is simple, and it is beautiful.', 'I will do justly, love mercy, and walk humbly with my God.', 'Father, thank You for showing me what is good. Help me act fairly, love mercy, and walk humbly with You today. Let my life reflect Your heart. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy052', 52, 'Proverbs 15:1', 'A soft answer turneth away wrath: but grievous words stir up anger.', 'A gentle answer can calm a tense moment, while harsh words stoke anger. Your tone can be a gift of peace.', 'I choose a soft answer. My words turn away wrath and bring peace instead of stirring up anger.', 'Lord, guard my mouth today. When conversations get tense, give me a gentle answer and a calm spirit. Let my words bring peace in my home and work. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy053', 53, 'Colossians 3:13-14', 'Forbearing one another, and forgiving one another, if any man have a quarrel against any: even as Christ forgave you, so also do ye. And above all these things put on charity, which is the bond of perfectness.', 'Forgiveness is not pretending nothing happened; it is choosing to release others as Christ released you. Love holds everything together.', 'I forbear and forgive others, even as Christ forgave me. Above all things I put on love, the bond of perfectness.', 'Jesus, You have forgiven me so much. Give me grace to bear with others and to release them. Clothe me with love that holds my relationships together. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy054', 54, 'Psalm 103:11-12', 'For as the heaven is high above the earth, so great is his mercy toward them that fear him. As far as the east is from the west, so far hath he removed our transgressions from us.', 'God''s mercy is as high as the heavens, and He has removed your sins as far as the east is from the west. You do not have to carry them.', 'God''s mercy toward me is as high as the heaven above the earth. He has removed my transgressions from me as far as the east is from the west.', 'Father, thank You for mercy greater than I can measure. Thank You for removing my sins so far away. Help me to stop picking up what You have taken away. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy055', 55, '1 Peter 4:8', 'And above all things have fervent charity among yourselves: for charity shall cover the multitude of sins.', 'Above everything, keep loving deeply. Fervent love chooses to cover offences rather than expose and repeat them.', 'Above all things, I have fervent love for others, for love covers a multitude of sins.', 'Lord, give me deep, fervent love for those around me. Help me cover offences with grace instead of keeping records. Let Your love lead my responses today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy056', 56, 'Galatians 6:2', 'Bear ye one another''s burdens, and so fulfil the law of Christ.', 'Someone near you is carrying something heavy. When you help bear their burden, you live out the law of Christ.', 'I bear the burdens of others, and in doing so I fulfil the law of Christ.', 'Father, open my eyes to the people carrying heavy loads. Show me how to help, listen, and pray with them. Let me fulfil the law of Christ through love. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy057', 57, '1 Thessalonians 5:11', 'Wherefore comfort yourselves together, and edify one another, even as also ye do.', 'Your words can build someone up today. Take a moment to comfort, encourage, and strengthen a brother or sister.', 'I comfort others and build them up. My words bring encouragement and strength to those around me.', 'Lord, make me an encourager. Bring someone to mind who needs comfort today, and give me the right words to build them up. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy058', 58, 'John 13:34-35', 'A new commandment I give unto you, That ye love one another; as I have loved you, that ye also love one another. By this shall all men know that ye are my disciples, if ye have love one to another.', 'Jesus said the world would recognise His followers by their love. Loving one another is our clearest witness.', 'I love others as Jesus has loved me. By this love, people will know that I am His disciple.', 'Jesus, thank You for loving me first. Help me love others the way You have loved me, so that my life points people to You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy059', 59, 'Romans 13:10', 'Love worketh no ill to his neighbour: therefore love is the fulfilling of the law.', 'Love does no harm to its neighbour. When you walk in love, you are fulfilling what God''s law was always pointing to.', 'My love works no ill toward my neighbour. By walking in love, I fulfil the law.', 'Father, as this month ends, keep me walking in love. Let my actions bring good, not harm, to everyone I meet. Fill me afresh with Your love. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy060', 60, 'Matthew 6:6', 'But thou, when thou prayest, enter into thy closet, and when thou hast shut thy door, pray to thy Father which is in secret; and thy Father which seeth in secret shall reward thee openly.', 'Prayer doesn’t need an audience or perfect words. A quiet, shut-door moment with your Father is seen and treasured by Him.', 'I have a secret place with my Father. He sees me when I pray in quiet, and He rewards the time I spend with Him.', 'Father, thank You that You see me in the secret place. Teach me to shut the door on noise and simply be with You. Meet me there today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy061', 61, 'James 4:8', 'Draw nigh to God, and he will draw nigh to you. Cleanse your hands, ye sinners; and purify your hearts, ye double minded.', 'God is not far off waiting for you to be perfect. Take one step toward Him, and He comes near to you.', 'I draw near to God today, and He draws near to me. He is making my hands clean and my heart whole and undivided.', 'Lord, I take a step toward You right now. Thank You for drawing near to me. Wash my hands, settle my divided heart, and make me wholly Yours. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy062', 62, 'Joel 2:12-13', 'Therefore also now, saith the LORD, turn ye even to me with all your heart, and with fasting, and with weeping, and with mourning: And rend your heart, and not your garments, and turn unto the LORD your God: for he is gracious and merciful, slow to anger, and of great kindness, and repenteth him of the evil.', 'God invites us back with our whole heart, not with outward show. He is gracious, merciful and slow to anger toward those who return.', 'I turn to the Lord with all my heart. He is gracious and merciful, slow to anger and of great kindness toward me.', 'Lord, I turn to You with my whole heart, not just my outward actions. Thank You for being gracious, merciful and kind. Tender my heart as I seek You in prayer and fasting. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy063', 63, 'Psalm 51:10', 'Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit within me.', 'You don’t have to fix your heart on your own. Ask God to create something clean and new inside you.', 'God is creating a clean heart in me and renewing a right spirit within me. I am not stuck; I am being made new.', 'O God, create in me a clean heart today. Renew a right spirit within me where I feel tired or tangled. I trust You to do what I cannot. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy064', 64, 'Deuteronomy 4:29', 'But if from thence thou shalt seek the LORD thy God, thou shalt find him, if thou seek him with all thy heart and with all thy soul.', 'Even from a far-off, difficult place, God can be found. He promises that a wholehearted search for Him will not end empty.', 'I seek the Lord my God with all my heart and with all my soul, and I shall find Him.', 'Lord my God, wherever I find myself today, I seek You with all my heart and soul. Thank You for Your promise that I will find You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy065', 65, 'Luke 15:20', 'And he arose, and came to his father. But when he was yet a great way off, his father saw him, and had compassion, and ran, and fell on his neck, and kissed him.', 'While the son was still far away, the father ran to him. However far you feel, God is already running toward you with compassion.', 'I arise and come to my Father. He sees me from afar, has compassion on me and welcomes me with open arms.', 'Father, I am coming home to You today. Thank You that You run toward me with compassion instead of waiting with a list. Hold me close and restore me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy066', 66, 'Hebrews 4:16', 'Let us therefore come boldly unto the throne of grace, that we may obtain mercy, and find grace to help in time of need.', 'Because of Jesus, God’s throne is a throne of grace. You can come boldly, not timidly, and find mercy and help right when you need it.', 'I come boldly to the throne of grace. I receive mercy and find grace to help me in my time of need.', 'Father, I come boldly before Your throne of grace because of Jesus. I receive Your mercy today and ask for grace to help me in every need I face. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy067', 67, '1 Peter 5:6-7', 'Humble yourselves therefore under the mighty hand of God, that he may exalt you in due time: Casting all your care upon him; for he careth for you.', 'Humility means letting God carry what you cannot. Cast every care on Him, because He truly cares for you, and trust His timing.', 'I humble myself under God’s mighty hand. I cast all my care upon Him, because He cares for me.', 'Lord, I bow under Your mighty hand and hand You every worry I have been carrying. Thank You that You care for me. I trust You to lift me up in due time. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy068', 68, 'Matthew 11:28-29', 'Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest. Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls.', 'Jesus is gentle and humble in heart. If you are weary and heavy laden, come to Him and learn His way of rest.', 'I come to Jesus with my heavy load. I take His yoke, learn from His gentle heart, and find rest for my soul.', 'Jesus, I am coming to You tired and heavy laden. Thank You that You are meek and lowly in heart. Teach me Your ways and give my soul Your rest. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy069', 69, 'Psalm 145:18', 'The LORD is nigh unto all them that call upon him, to all that call upon him in truth.', 'The Lord is near to all who call on Him honestly. You don’t need polished words, just a true heart.', 'The Lord is near to me when I call upon Him in truth. I call on Him today and He is close.', 'Lord, I call upon You in truth right now, just as I am. Thank You that You are near to me. Let me feel Your nearness through this whole day. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy070', 70, 'Nehemiah 8:10', 'Then he said unto them, Go your way, eat the fat, and drink the sweet, and send portions unto them for whom nothing is prepared: for this day is holy unto our LORD: neither be ye sorry; for the joy of the LORD is your strength.', 'When God’s people wept over His word, they were told not to be sorry but to celebrate and share. His joy becomes their strength.', 'This day is holy unto the Lord. I will not be sorrowful, for the joy of the Lord is my strength.', 'Lord, lift the heaviness from my heart today. Let Your joy be my strength, and make me generous toward anyone who has nothing prepared. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy071', 71, 'Hosea 6:1', 'Come, and let us return unto the LORD: for he hath torn, and he will heal us; he hath smitten, and he will bind us up.', 'Returning to God is returning to the One who heals. Whatever has wounded you, He knows how to bind it up.', 'I return to the Lord today. He will heal me and bind up what has been broken in me.', 'Lord, I come back to You. Where I am hurting, heal me; where I am broken, bind me up. Thank You that returning to You is always the way to restoration. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy072', 72, 'Romans 12:1', 'I beseech you therefore, brethren, by the mercies of God, that ye present your bodies a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable unto God, which is your reasonable service.', 'Surrender is not a single moment but a daily offering. In light of God’s mercies, we give Him our whole lives as worship.', 'Because of God’s mercies, I present my life to Him as a living sacrifice, holy and acceptable to Him.', 'Father, in view of all Your mercies, I offer You my body, my time and my choices today. Make my ordinary life an act of worship that pleases You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy073', 73, 'Philippians 4:6-7', 'Be careful for nothing; but in every thing by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving let your requests be made known unto God. And the peace of God, which passeth all understanding, shall keep your hearts and minds through Christ Jesus.', 'Turn every worry into a prayer with thanksgiving. God’s peace, deeper than understanding, will guard your heart and mind in Christ.', 'I bring every request to God with thanksgiving. His peace, which passes understanding, keeps my heart and mind through Christ Jesus.', 'Father, I lay my requests before You with a thankful heart. Instead of anxiety, fill me with Your peace. Guard my heart and mind in Christ Jesus today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy074', 74, 'Isaiah 55:6', 'Seek ye the LORD while he may be found, call ye upon him while he is near:', 'God is near and ready to be found. Today is a good day to seek Him and call on His name.', 'I seek the Lord today while He may be found. I call upon Him, for He is near.', 'Lord, I seek You today with an open heart. Thank You that You are near and willing to be found. I call upon Your name; draw me closer to You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy075', 75, 'Psalm 46:10', 'Be still, and know that I am God: I will be exalted among the heathen, I will be exalted in the earth.', 'Stillness is not doing nothing; it is remembering who God is. Pause, breathe, and let Him be God over your day.', 'I am still, and I know that He is God. He will be exalted in the earth and in my life.', 'Lord, quiet the rush inside me. Help me be still and know that You are God. Be exalted in my heart, my home and my day. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy076', 76, 'Matthew 6:17-18', 'But thou, when thou fastest, anoint thine head, and wash thy face; That thou appear not unto men to fast, but unto thy Father which is in secret: and thy Father, which seeth in secret, shall reward thee openly.', 'Fasting is a private conversation with your Father, not a performance. He sees what is done in secret and honours it.', 'When I fast, I do it for my Father who sees in secret, and my Father who sees in secret will reward me openly.', 'Father, let my seeking of You be sincere and quiet, not for show. Thank You that You see in secret. Draw me closer to You as I set time apart for You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy077', 77, 'Luke 11:9', 'And I say unto you, Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you.', 'Jesus invites persistent, trusting prayer. Keep asking, keep seeking, keep knocking; your Father is listening.', 'I ask, and it shall be given me; I seek, and I shall find; I knock, and it shall be opened unto me.', 'Father, I come asking, seeking and knocking today. Thank You that You hear me and respond as a good Father. Give me patience and faith to keep praying. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy078', 78, '2 Chronicles 7:14', 'If my people, which are called by my name, shall humble themselves, and pray, and seek my face, and turn from their wicked ways; then will I hear from heaven, and will forgive their sin, and will heal their land.', 'God’s promise to His people was clear: humility, prayer and seeking His face open the way to forgiveness and healing.', 'I humble myself, pray and seek God’s face. He hears from heaven, forgives, and brings healing.', 'Lord, I humble myself before You and seek Your face. Forgive me where I have wandered and turn my heart fully to You. Bring Your healing to my life and my land. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy079', 79, 'Psalm 73:28', 'But it is good for me to draw near to God: I have put my trust in the Lord GOD, that I may declare all thy works.', 'Drawing near to God is simply good for us. Trust Him, and let your life become a story of what He has done.', 'It is good for me to draw near to God. I have put my trust in the Lord GOD, and I will declare all His works.', 'Lord GOD, it is good to be near You. I put my trust in You again today. Give me a grateful heart and a ready voice to tell of all Your works. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy080', 80, 'Zechariah 1:3', 'Therefore say thou unto them, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Turn ye unto me, saith the LORD of hosts, and I will turn unto you, saith the LORD of hosts.', 'God’s invitation is simple and warm: turn to Me, and I will turn to you. He meets every returning heart.', 'I turn to the Lord of hosts, and He turns to me. His face is toward me today.', 'Lord of hosts, I turn my heart to You today. Thank You for the promise that You turn toward me. Let me walk this day with Your face shining on me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.');
INSERT INTO devotions (id, sort, reference, text, reflection, declaration, prayer) VALUES
 ('dy081', 81, 'Proverbs 11:2', 'When pride cometh, then cometh shame: but with the lowly is wisdom.', 'Pride sets us up to fall, but humility makes room for wisdom. A lowly heart is a teachable heart.', 'I walk in lowliness of heart, and with the lowly is wisdom. I choose humility and receive wisdom today.', 'Lord, guard me from pride and give me a humble, teachable spirit. Fill me with Your wisdom as I walk lowly before You and kindly with others. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy082', 82, 'Luke 22:42', 'Saying, Father, if thou be willing, remove this cup from me: nevertheless not my will, but thine, be done.', 'In His hardest hour, Jesus prayed honestly and still surrendered. You can tell God what you want and still trust His will.', 'Like Jesus, I bring my honest desires to the Father, and I say, not my will, but Yours, be done.', 'Father, You know what I want and what I fear. I bring it all honestly to You. Yet, like Jesus, I pray: not my will, but Yours be done. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy083', 83, '1 Samuel 3:10', 'And the LORD came, and stood, and called as at other times, Samuel, Samuel. Then Samuel answered, Speak; for thy servant heareth.', 'God called Samuel by name, and Samuel answered with a surrendered, listening heart. Surrender often begins with simply saying, Speak, Lord.', 'The Lord calls me, and I answer: Speak, Lord, for Your servant is listening.', 'Lord, You know my name and You still speak. Quiet my heart so I can hear You. Speak, Lord, for Your servant is listening, and help me obey. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy084', 84, 'Isaiah 30:15', 'For thus saith the Lord GOD, the Holy One of Israel; In returning and rest shall ye be saved; in quietness and in confidence shall be your strength: and ye would not.', 'God’s strength is often found not in striving, but in returning to Him, resting, and trusting quietly.', 'In returning and rest I am saved; in quietness and in confidence is my strength.', 'Lord, I return to You and rest. Replace my striving with quiet confidence in You. Be my strength today as I trust You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy085', 85, 'Psalm 62:8', 'Trust in him at all times; ye people, pour out your heart before him: God is a refuge for us. Selah.', 'You can trust God at all times and pour out everything in your heart to Him. He is a safe refuge.', 'I trust in God at all times. I pour out my heart before Him, for God is my refuge.', 'Father, I pour out my heart before You now, all of it. Thank You that You are my refuge and it is safe to trust You at all times. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy086', 86, 'Jeremiah 33:3', 'Call unto me, and I will answer thee, and shew thee great and mighty things, which thou knowest not.', 'God invites you to call, and promises to answer and reveal great things you do not yet know.', 'I call unto the Lord, and He answers me and shows me great and mighty things which I know not.', 'Lord, I call to You today. Thank You for Your promise to answer. Open my eyes to the great and mighty things You want to show me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy087', 87, 'Isaiah 44:22', 'I have blotted out, as a thick cloud, thy transgressions, and, as a cloud, thy sins: return unto me; for I have redeemed thee.', 'God has blotted out your sins like a cloud that vanishes. He invites you to return because He has already redeemed you.', 'My transgressions are blotted out like a thick cloud. I return to the Lord, for He has redeemed me.', 'Lord, thank You for blotting out my sins like a cloud that disappears. I return to You with gratitude, knowing I am redeemed. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy088', 88, 'Mark 1:35', 'And in the morning, rising up a great while before day, he went out, and departed into a solitary place, and there prayed.', 'Even Jesus made space to pray before the day began. A few quiet moments with God can shape everything that follows.', 'Like Jesus, I make room to meet with my Father. I start my day in His presence.', 'Father, thank You for this new morning. Like Jesus, I want to begin my day with You. Help me find quiet places to pray and hear Your voice. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy089', 89, 'Psalm 25:9', 'The meek will he guide in judgment: and the meek will he teach his way.', 'God delights to guide and teach humble hearts. When you admit you need direction, He leads you in His way.', 'I walk in meekness, and the Lord guides me in judgment and teaches me His way.', 'Lord, I come to You humbly, needing Your direction. Guide me in right judgment and teach me Your way today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy090', 90, 'Hosea 14:4', 'I will heal their backsliding, I will love them freely: for mine anger is turned away from him.', 'God’s answer to His wandering people is healing, not rejection. He loves freely and turns His anger away.', 'The Lord heals my backsliding and loves me freely. His anger is turned away from me.', 'Father, thank You that You heal my wandering heart and love me freely. I come back to You without fear, resting in Your kindness. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy091', 91, 'Isaiah 53:5', 'But he was wounded for our transgressions, he was bruised for our iniquities: the chastisement of our peace was upon him; and with his stripes we are healed.', 'Centuries before the cross, God described the Servant who would take our punishment. His wounds bring us peace and healing.', 'Jesus was wounded for my transgressions and bruised for my iniquities. The punishment that brings my peace was on Him, and by His stripes I am healed.', 'Lord Jesus, thank You for bearing the wounds that were meant for me. Because of You I have peace with God. Let Your healing reach every part of my life. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy092', 92, '1 Peter 2:24', 'Who his own self bare our sins in his own body on the tree, that we, being dead to sins, should live unto righteousness: by whose stripes ye were healed.', 'Jesus carried our sins in His own body on the cross so that we could be free from sin and live for what is right.', 'Jesus bore my sins in His own body on the tree. I am dead to sins and alive to righteousness, and by His stripes I am healed.', 'Jesus, thank You for carrying my sins on the cross. Help me live today as one who is free from sin and alive to righteousness. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy093', 93, 'Ephesians 2:8-9', 'For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves: it is the gift of God: Not of works, lest any man should boast.', 'Salvation is a gift, not a wage. You receive it by faith, not by working hard enough to earn it.', 'I am saved by grace through faith. It is the gift of God, not something I earned by my works.', 'Father, thank You for the gift of salvation that I could never earn. I rest in Your grace today instead of striving. Let my life overflow with gratitude. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy094', 94, 'Exodus 12:13', 'And the blood shall be to you for a token upon the houses where ye are: and when I see the blood, I will pass over you, and the plague shall not be upon you to destroy you, when I smite the land of Egypt.', 'On Passover night, the blood on the doorposts meant judgment passed over. Jesus is our Passover Lamb, and His blood covers all who trust Him.', 'Jesus is my Passover Lamb. When God sees the blood, He passes over, and destruction shall not be upon me.', 'Father, thank You for the blood of Jesus, the Lamb who was slain for me. I shelter under His sacrifice today and rest in Your protection. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy095', 95, 'John 19:30', 'When Jesus therefore had received the vinegar, he said, It is finished: and he bowed his head, and gave up the ghost.', 'It is finished. Jesus completed the work of salvation on the cross. Nothing needs to be added to what He has done.', 'Jesus said, It is finished. I rest in His finished work on the cross for me.', 'Lord Jesus, thank You for finishing the work on the cross. I stop trying to add to it and simply trust what You have done for me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy096', 96, 'Hebrews 12:2', 'Looking unto Jesus the author and finisher of our faith; who for the joy that was set before him endured the cross, despising the shame, and is set down at the right hand of the throne of God.', 'Keep your eyes on Jesus. He endured the cross for the joy ahead and now sits at God’s right hand, finishing what He began in you.', 'I look to Jesus, the author and finisher of my faith, who endured the cross for joy and is seated at God’s right hand.', 'Jesus, I fix my eyes on You today. Thank You for enduring the cross and despising its shame for me. Author and finish my faith. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy097', 97, 'Galatians 2:20', 'I am crucified with Christ: nevertheless I live; yet not I, but Christ liveth in me: and the life which I now live in the flesh I live by the faith of the Son of God, who loved me, and gave himself for me.', 'The old me was crucified with Christ. Now Christ lives in me, and I live by faith in the One who loved me and gave Himself for me.', 'I am crucified with Christ, yet I live; Christ lives in me. I live by faith in the Son of God, who loved me and gave Himself for me.', 'Lord Jesus, thank You for loving me and giving Yourself for me. Live Your life through me today. Help me walk by faith in You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy098', 98, 'Hosea 6:2', 'After two days will he revive us: in the third day he will raise us up, and we shall live in his sight.', 'Hosea spoke of God reviving His people on the third day. Through Jesus, raised on the third day, we are given new life to live before God.', 'The Lord revives me and raises me up, and I shall live in His sight.', 'Lord, revive me where I feel worn down. Raise me up into the new life You give, and let me live every moment in Your sight. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy099', 99, 'Matthew 28:6', 'He is not here: for he is risen, as he said. Come, see the place where the Lord lay.', 'The tomb is empty! Jesus rose just as He said He would. His promises are true, and death could not hold Him.', 'Jesus is not in the tomb; He is risen, as He said. I serve a living Saviour who keeps His word.', 'Risen Lord, thank You that the tomb is empty and You are alive, just as You said. Fill me with the joy and hope of Your resurrection today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy100', 100, 'John 11:25', 'Jesus said unto her, I am the resurrection, and the life: he that believeth in me, though he were dead, yet shall he live:', 'Jesus doesn’t just give resurrection and life; He is resurrection and life. Whoever believes in Him will live, even through death.', 'Jesus is the resurrection and the life. I believe in Him, and though I die, yet shall I live.', 'Jesus, You are the resurrection and the life. I believe in You. Thank You that death is not the end for those who trust You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy101', 101, '1 Corinthians 15:55-57', 'O death, where is thy sting? O grave, where is thy victory? The sting of death is sin; and the strength of sin is the law. But thanks be to God, which giveth us the victory through our Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Death has lost its sting because Jesus dealt with sin. Through Him, God gives us the victory.', 'Death has no sting and the grave has no victory over me. Thanks be to God, who gives me the victory through my Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Father, thank You that through Jesus death has lost its sting and the grave its victory. I receive the victory You give me in Christ today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy102', 102, 'Romans 6:4', 'Therefore we are buried with him by baptism into death: that like as Christ was raised up from the dead by the glory of the Father, even so we also should walk in newness of life.', 'Just as Christ was raised from the dead, we too are raised to walk in a completely new kind of life.', 'I am buried with Christ and raised with Him. As Christ was raised by the glory of the Father, I walk in newness of life.', 'Father, thank You that I share in Christ’s death and resurrection. Help me walk in newness of life today, step by step, by Your grace. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy103', 103, 'Colossians 3:1', 'If ye then be risen with Christ, seek those things which are above, where Christ sitteth on the right hand of God.', 'Because you are raised with Christ, lift your eyes. Set your heart on the things above, where Jesus reigns.', 'I am risen with Christ, so I seek those things which are above, where Christ sits at the right hand of God.', 'Lord, lift my eyes above the worries of today. Since I am risen with Christ, help me seek the things above where He reigns. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy104', 104, 'Romans 8:1', 'There is therefore now no condemnation to them which are in Christ Jesus, who walk not after the flesh, but after the Spirit.', 'If you are in Christ Jesus, there is no condemnation for you. You can walk by the Spirit free from shame.', 'There is now no condemnation for me, because I am in Christ Jesus. I walk after the Spirit.', 'Father, thank You that there is no condemnation for me in Christ Jesus. Quiet every accusing voice and help me walk after the Spirit today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy105', 105, '2 Corinthians 12:9', 'And he said unto me, My grace is sufficient for thee: for my strength is made perfect in weakness. Most gladly therefore will I rather glory in my infirmities, that the power of Christ may rest upon me.', 'Your weakness is not a barrier to God. His grace is enough, and His strength shows up most in the places you feel weakest.', 'God’s grace is sufficient for me. His strength is made perfect in my weakness, and the power of Christ rests upon me.', 'Lord, You know where I feel weak today. Thank You that Your grace is enough for me. Let Your strength be made perfect in my weakness. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy106', 106, 'Titus 2:11', 'For the grace of God that bringeth salvation hath appeared to all men,', 'God’s saving grace has appeared in Jesus, and it is offered to everyone. No one is outside its reach, including you.', 'The grace of God that brings salvation has appeared, and it has reached me.', 'Father, thank You that Your saving grace has appeared in Jesus for all people, including me. Let Your grace shape how I think, speak and live today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy107', 107, '1 John 1:9', 'If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.', 'You never have to hide from God. When we confess our sins, He is faithful to forgive and completely cleanse us.', 'When I confess my sins, God is faithful and just to forgive me and to cleanse me from all unrighteousness.', 'Father, I bring You my sins honestly, holding nothing back. Thank You that You are faithful and just to forgive me and cleanse me completely. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy108', 108, 'Romans 6:14', 'For sin shall not have dominion over you: for ye are not under the law, but under grace.', 'Under grace, sin is no longer your master. God’s grace doesn’t just pardon you; it breaks sin’s rule over your life.', 'Sin shall not have dominion over me, for I am not under the law, but under grace.', 'Lord, thank You that I live under grace and sin is no longer my master. Strengthen me by Your grace to walk free today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy109', 109, '1 Peter 1:3', 'Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, which according to his abundant mercy hath begotten us again unto a lively hope by the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead,', 'Because Jesus rose from the dead, God has given us new birth into a living hope, a hope that is alive and growing.', 'By His abundant mercy, God has begotten me again unto a lively hope by the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead.', 'Blessed be You, Father, for Your abundant mercy. Thank You for new birth and a living hope through the resurrection of Jesus. Let that hope rise in me today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy110', 110, 'Luke 24:5-6', 'And as they were afraid, and bowed down their faces to the earth, they said unto them, Why seek ye the living among the dead? He is not here, but is risen: remember how he spake unto you when he was yet in Galilee,', 'The women came to a tomb looking for a dead body, but Jesus was alive. Stop searching among the dead for the living Lord.', 'I do not seek the living among the dead. Jesus is not here; He is risen, just as He said.', 'Risen Jesus, lift my face from fear and sorrow. Help me remember Your words and rejoice that You are alive. I seek You as my living Lord today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy111', 111, 'Colossians 2:14', 'Blotting out the handwriting of ordinances that was against us, which was contrary to us, and took it out of the way, nailing it to his cross;', 'Everything written against us, Jesus took out of the way and nailed to His cross. The record is cancelled.', 'The handwriting that was against me has been blotted out. Jesus took it out of the way, nailing it to His cross.', 'Lord Jesus, thank You for nailing to the cross everything that stood against me. I walk in the freedom of a cancelled record today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy112', 112, 'Revelation 1:18', 'I am he that liveth, and was dead; and, behold, I am alive for evermore, Amen; and have the keys of hell and of death.', 'Jesus was dead and is now alive forevermore. He holds the keys of death and hell, so you can face every tomorrow without fear.', 'My Jesus lives, was dead, and is alive for evermore. He holds the keys of hell and of death.', 'Lord Jesus, You are alive for evermore and You hold the keys of death and hell. Thank You that I do not need to fear. I trust my life to You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy113', 113, 'Romans 8:11', 'But if the Spirit of him that raised up Jesus from the dead dwell in you, he that raised up Christ from the dead shall also quicken your mortal bodies by his Spirit that dwelleth in you.', 'The same Spirit who raised Jesus from the dead lives in every believer, bringing His life into our mortal bodies.', 'The Spirit of Him who raised Jesus from the dead dwells in me, and He gives life to my mortal body by His Spirit.', 'Father, thank You that the Spirit who raised Jesus from the dead dwells in me. Breathe Your life into me today, body and soul. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy114', 114, 'Ephesians 2:4-5', 'But God, who is rich in mercy, for his great love wherewith he loved us, Even when we were dead in sins, hath quickened us together with Christ, (by grace ye are saved;)', 'When we were dead in sin, God, rich in mercy, made us alive with Christ. That is the heart of grace.', 'God is rich in mercy toward me. Even when I was dead in sins, He made me alive together with Christ. By grace I am saved.', 'Father, rich in mercy, thank You for Your great love. When I was dead in sins, You made me alive with Christ. I rejoice in Your grace today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy115', 115, 'John 10:10', 'The thief cometh not, but for to steal, and to kill, and to destroy: I am come that they might have life, and that they might have it more abundantly.', 'The enemy comes to steal, kill and destroy, but Jesus came to give life, full and overflowing.', 'Jesus came that I might have life, and have it more abundantly. I receive His life today.', 'Jesus, thank You for coming to give me abundant life. Guard me from everything that steals and destroys, and fill me with Your life today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy116', 116, 'Isaiah 1:18', 'Come now, and let us reason together, saith the LORD: though your sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow; though they be red like crimson, they shall be as wool.', 'God invites you to come and talk with Him. However deep the stain, His cleansing makes you white as snow.', 'The Lord invites me to come. Though my sins were as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow.', 'Lord, I accept Your invitation to come and reason with You. Thank You that You wash even scarlet stains white as snow. I receive Your cleansing today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy117', 117, 'Romans 6:11', 'Likewise reckon ye also yourselves to be dead indeed unto sin, but alive unto God through Jesus Christ our Lord.', 'Count it as true: you are dead to sin and alive to God in Christ. Let what God says about you shape how you see yourself.', 'I reckon myself dead indeed unto sin, but alive unto God through Jesus Christ my Lord.', 'Father, help me see myself the way You see me: dead to sin and alive to You in Christ. Let this truth guide my choices today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy118', 118, '1 John 5:4', 'For whatsoever is born of God overcometh the world: and this is the victory that overcometh the world, even our faith.', 'Everyone born of God overcomes the world, and the victory comes through faith in Jesus, not through our own strength.', 'I am born of God, and whatever is born of God overcomes the world. My faith is the victory that overcomes the world.', 'Father, thank You that I am born of You. Strengthen my faith in Jesus today, the victory that overcomes the world. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy119', 119, 'Hebrews 2:14-15', 'Forasmuch then as the children are partakers of flesh and blood, he also himself likewise took part of the same; that through death he might destroy him that had the power of death, that is, the devil; And deliver them who through fear of death were all their lifetime subject to bondage.', 'Jesus became human and, through His death, broke the devil’s power and freed us from lifelong fear of death.', 'Jesus shared in flesh and blood and through His death destroyed the power of the devil. I am delivered from the fear of death.', 'Lord Jesus, thank You for becoming one of us and breaking the power of death. Set me free from every bondage of fear today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy120', 120, 'Philippians 3:10', 'That I may know him, and the power of his resurrection, and the fellowship of his sufferings, being made conformable unto his death;', 'Paul’s deepest desire was simply to know Jesus: His resurrection power and His sufferings. Knowing Him is the goal of the whole journey.', 'I want to know Jesus and the power of His resurrection, and to share in the fellowship of His sufferings.', 'Jesus, more than anything I want to know You. Let me experience the power of Your resurrection and walk closely with You in every season. In Jesus'' name, Amen.');
INSERT INTO devotions (id, sort, reference, text, reflection, declaration, prayer) VALUES
 ('dy121', 121, 'John 14:16-17', 'And I will pray the Father, and he shall give you another Comforter, that he may abide with you for ever; Even the Spirit of truth; whom the world cannot receive, because it seeth him not, neither knoweth him: but ye know him; for he dwelleth with you, and shall be in you.', 'Jesus did not leave us alone. The Holy Spirit, our Comforter, lives with us and in us, today and for ever.', 'I am not alone. The Comforter, the Spirit of truth, dwells with me and in me, and He abides with me for ever.', 'Father, thank You for sending the Comforter to abide with me. Help me to know Him more and to lean on His presence through this day. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy122', 122, 'Acts 1:8', 'But ye shall receive power, after that the Holy Ghost is come upon you: and ye shall be witnesses unto me both in Jerusalem, and in all Judaea, and in Samaria, and unto the uttermost part of the earth.', 'The Holy Spirit gives power, not so we can impress people, but so our lives can point others to Jesus wherever we go.', 'I receive power as the Holy Ghost comes upon me, and I am a witness for Jesus right where I am today.', 'Lord, fill me with the power of Your Holy Spirit. Make my words and my life a gentle, bold witness to Jesus in my home, my work and my city. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy123', 123, 'Romans 8:26', 'Likewise the Spirit also helpeth our infirmities: for we know not what we should pray for as we ought: but the Spirit itself maketh intercession for us with groanings which cannot be uttered.', 'When you do not know what to pray, you are not failing. The Spirit Himself helps your weakness and prays for you beyond words.', 'When I don''t know what to pray, the Spirit helps me. He intercedes for me, and my weakness is held in His care.', 'Holy Spirit, thank You for helping me when words run out. Pray through me today, and let my sighs become prayers before the Father. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy124', 124, 'Galatians 5:22-23', 'But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, longsuffering, gentleness, goodness, faith, Meekness, temperance: against such there is no law.', 'Fruit grows slowly and quietly. As we stay close to God, the Spirit grows love, joy, peace and self-control in us.', 'I am a branch where the Spirit grows fruit: love, joy, peace, patience, gentleness, goodness, faith, meekness and self-control.', 'Father, let the fruit of Your Spirit grow in me today. Where I am short on patience or joy, fill me with Yours. Make my life sweet to those around me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy125', 125, 'John 16:13', 'Howbeit when he, the Spirit of truth, is come, he will guide you into all truth: for he shall not speak of himself; but whatsoever he shall hear, that shall he speak: and he will shew you things to come.', 'You do not have to figure everything out alone. The Spirit of truth guides you step by step into all truth.', 'The Spirit of truth guides me into all truth. I will not walk in confusion; I will listen and follow His leading.', 'Holy Spirit, guide me into truth today. Quiet the noise around me so I can hear You clearly, and give me courage to follow where You lead. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy126', 126, 'Zechariah 4:6', 'Then he answered and spake unto me, saying, This is the word of the LORD unto Zerubbabel, saying, Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith the LORD of hosts.', 'Some things cannot be pushed through by strength or effort. God finishes His work in us by His Spirit.', 'Not by might, nor by power, but by the Spirit of the Lord. I rest from striving and trust His Spirit to do what I cannot.', 'Lord of hosts, I lay down my own striving. Let Your Spirit do the work that my strength cannot. Give me peace as I trust You today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy127', 127, 'Romans 8:14', 'For as many as are led by the Spirit of God, they are the sons of God.', 'Being led by the Spirit is a mark of belonging. You are not a stranger to God; you are His child.', 'I am led by the Spirit of God, and I am a child of God. I belong in my Father''s family.', 'Father, thank You for making me Your child. Lead me by Your Spirit in every choice today, and let me walk with the confidence of one who belongs to You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy128', 128, '2 Timothy 1:7', 'For God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind.', 'Fear is not from God. His Spirit gives us power to act, love to guide us, and a sound, steady mind.', 'God has not given me a spirit of fear. I have power, love and a sound mind.', 'Father, where fear has been speaking loudly, let Your Spirit speak louder. Fill me with power, love and a sound mind as I face this day. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy129', 129, 'Job 33:4', 'The spirit of God hath made me, and the breath of the Almighty hath given me life.', 'The same Spirit who formed you is the one who keeps breathing life into you. Your life is His gift and His work.', 'The Spirit of God has made me, and the breath of the Almighty has given me life. I live today by His breath.', 'Father, thank You that Your Spirit made me and Your breath gives me life. Fill my lungs and my heart afresh today, and let me live for You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy130', 130, 'Romans 15:13', 'Now the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace in believing, that ye may abound in hope, through the power of the Holy Ghost.', 'Hope is not something we have to manufacture. The God of hope fills us with joy and peace as we trust Him.', 'The God of hope fills me with joy and peace as I believe, and by the power of the Holy Ghost I overflow with hope.', 'God of hope, fill me with joy and peace today as I trust You. Let hope overflow from me by the power of Your Holy Spirit. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy131', 131, 'John 14:26', 'But the Comforter, which is the Holy Ghost, whom the Father will send in my name, he shall teach you all things, and bring all things to your remembrance, whatsoever I have said unto you.', 'The Holy Spirit is our Teacher. He brings the words of Jesus back to our minds right when we need them.', 'The Holy Ghost teaches me all things and brings Jesus'' words to my remembrance when I need them.', 'Holy Spirit, be my Teacher today. Remind me of the words of Jesus in every conversation and decision, and help me to live them out. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy132', 132, '1 Corinthians 3:16', 'Know ye not that ye are the temple of God, and that the Spirit of God dwelleth in you?', 'You are God''s dwelling place. The Spirit of God lives in you, which makes your life sacred and deeply valued.', 'I am the temple of God, and the Spirit of God dwells in me. My life is His home.', 'Father, thank You for choosing to live in me by Your Spirit. Help me to honour You with my body, my thoughts and my days. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy133', 133, 'Jude 1:20-21', 'But ye, beloved, building up yourselves on your most holy faith, praying in the Holy Ghost, Keep yourselves in the love of God, looking for the mercy of our Lord Jesus Christ unto eternal life.', 'Praying in the Holy Ghost builds us up. It keeps us close to God''s love while we wait for His mercy.', 'I build myself up on my most holy faith, praying in the Holy Ghost, and I keep myself in the love of God.', 'Lord, teach me to pray in the Holy Ghost. Build up my faith today and keep me close in Your love as I look to Your mercy. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy134', 134, 'Romans 5:5', 'And hope maketh not ashamed; because the love of God is shed abroad in our hearts by the Holy Ghost which is given unto us.', 'Our hope in God will not leave us embarrassed. The Holy Spirit pours God''s love into our hearts.', 'My hope will not put me to shame, because the love of God is poured into my heart by the Holy Ghost.', 'Father, pour Your love into my heart afresh by Your Holy Spirit. Let that love steady my hope and flow out to others today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy135', 135, 'Galatians 5:16', 'This I say then, Walk in the Spirit, and ye shall not fulfil the lust of the flesh.', 'Freedom from old patterns comes not by fighting harder but by walking closely with the Spirit, one step at a time.', 'I walk in the Spirit today, and I will not fulfil the desires of the flesh.', 'Holy Spirit, I choose to walk with You today. Lead each step and give me strength to say no to what pulls me away from God. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy136', 136, 'Luke 11:13', 'If ye then, being evil, know how to give good gifts unto your children: how much more shall your heavenly Father give the Holy Spirit to them that ask him?', 'Your heavenly Father is a better giver than any earthly parent. He gladly gives the Holy Spirit to those who ask.', 'My heavenly Father gives the Holy Spirit to those who ask Him. I ask, and I receive from a generous Father.', 'Father, I ask You today for more of Your Holy Spirit. Thank You that You are a good Father who loves to give. Fill me afresh. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy137', 137, 'Acts 2:4', 'And they were all filled with the Holy Ghost, and began to speak with other tongues, as the Spirit gave them utterance.', 'On Pentecost the Spirit filled ordinary people and gave them words beyond their own. He still fills and empowers His people today.', 'I open my heart to be filled with the Holy Ghost, and I speak as the Spirit gives me utterance.', 'Lord Jesus, as You filled Your disciples at Pentecost, fill me with Your Holy Spirit. Let my words today be given by Your Spirit and bring glory to You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy138', 138, '2 Corinthians 3:17', 'Now the Lord is that Spirit: and where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is liberty.', 'Where the Spirit of the Lord is present, chains loosen. His presence brings freedom from fear, shame and old ways.', 'The Spirit of the Lord is with me, and where He is there is liberty. I walk in freedom today.', 'Lord, let Your Spirit bring liberty into every tight and troubled place in my life. Set my heart free to love and serve You joyfully. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy139', 139, 'Romans 8:16', 'The Spirit itself beareth witness with our spirit, that we are the children of God:', 'On days when you doubt, the Spirit quietly assures your heart: you really are a child of God.', 'The Spirit Himself bears witness with my spirit that I am a child of God.', 'Father, let Your Spirit whisper deep assurance to my heart today. When doubts come, remind me that I am Your child. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy140', 140, 'Ephesians 3:16', 'That he would grant you, according to the riches of his glory, to be strengthened with might by his Spirit in the inner man;', 'God''s strength works from the inside out. His Spirit strengthens the inner you, even when the outside feels weak.', 'According to the riches of His glory, I am strengthened with might by His Spirit in my inner man.', 'Father, from the riches of Your glory, strengthen me inside by Your Spirit. Where I feel worn out, pour in Your might and steady my heart. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy141', 141, 'Galatians 5:25', 'If we live in the Spirit, let us also walk in the Spirit.', 'The Spirit gave us new life; now we keep in step with Him in our daily choices, habits and relationships.', 'I live in the Spirit, so I will walk in the Spirit, keeping in step with Him today.', 'Holy Spirit, You have given me life. Help me to keep in step with You in my words, my choices and the way I treat others today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy142', 142, 'Isaiah 11:2', 'And the spirit of the LORD shall rest upon him, the spirit of wisdom and understanding, the spirit of counsel and might, the spirit of knowledge and of the fear of the LORD;', 'This Spirit of wisdom, counsel and might rested fully on Jesus. Through Christ, that same Spirit helps us today.', 'The Spirit who rested on Jesus is the Spirit of wisdom, understanding, counsel and might, and I look to Him for help today.', 'Lord Jesus, the Spirit of wisdom and might rested on You. By Your Spirit, give me understanding, good counsel and holy reverence in all I do today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy143', 143, 'Acts 13:52', 'And the disciples were filled with joy, and with the Holy Ghost.', 'Even after opposition, the disciples were filled with joy and with the Holy Ghost. His presence brings joy that circumstances cannot steal.', 'I am filled with joy and with the Holy Ghost, and my joy rests on His presence, not on my circumstances.', 'Holy Spirit, fill me today as You filled the first disciples. Let Your joy rise in me, even in hard places, and let it overflow to others. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy144', 144, 'Ephesians 5:18-19', 'And be not drunk with wine, wherein is excess; but be filled with the Spirit; Speaking to yourselves in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing and making melody in your heart to the Lord;', 'Instead of reaching for things that numb us, we can be filled with the Spirit, and songs of praise rise in our hearts.', 'I am filled with the Spirit, and I make melody in my heart to the Lord with psalms, hymns and spiritual songs.', 'Lord, fill me with Your Spirit today. Put a new song in my heart, and let praise carry me through every task and every hour. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy145', 145, 'Joel 2:28', 'And it shall come to pass afterward, that I will pour out my spirit upon all flesh; and your sons and your daughters shall prophesy, your old men shall dream dreams, your young men shall see visions:', 'God promised to pour out His Spirit on all kinds of people, young and old. No one is too ordinary for His Spirit.', 'God pours out His Spirit upon all flesh, and I am not left out. His Spirit gives dreams and vision to His people.', 'Father, thank You for pouring out Your Spirit on sons and daughters, young and old. Pour Your Spirit on me and my household, and give us godly dreams and vision. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy146', 146, 'Psalm 139:7-8', 'Whither shall I go from thy spirit? or whither shall I flee from thy presence? If I ascend up into heaven, thou art there: if I make my bed in hell, behold, thou art there.', 'There is no place you can go where God''s Spirit is absent. Even in the lowest places, He is there.', 'I can never go beyond God''s Spirit or presence. In the heights and in the depths, He is there with me.', 'Lord, thank You that I can never wander beyond Your presence. Wherever today takes me, high or low, remind me that You are there. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy147', 147, 'John 7:38-39', 'He that believeth on me, as the scripture hath said, out of his belly shall flow rivers of living water. (But this spake he of the Spirit, which they that believe on him should receive: for the Holy Ghost was not yet given; because that Jesus was not yet glorified.)', 'Jesus promised that the Spirit would flow from believers like rivers of living water, refreshing us and others.', 'I believe in Jesus, and out of me flow rivers of living water by His Spirit.', 'Lord Jesus, I believe in You. Let Your Spirit flow through me like living water, refreshing my own soul and everyone I meet today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy148', 148, 'Psalm 143:10', 'Teach me to do thy will; for thou art my God: thy spirit is good; lead me into the land of uprightness.', 'David asked God to teach and lead him. We can pray the same: God''s Spirit is good and leads us on level ground.', 'The Lord is my God. His Spirit is good, and He teaches me to do His will and leads me into the land of uprightness.', 'Lord, teach me to do Your will, for You are my God. Let Your good Spirit lead me on level ground today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy149', 149, 'Ephesians 6:18', 'Praying always with all prayer and supplication in the Spirit, and watching thereunto with all perseverance and supplication for all saints;', 'Prayer in the Spirit is not only for church meetings. We can pray at all times and keep watch for one another.', 'I pray always in the Spirit, with perseverance, and I lift up God''s people in prayer.', 'Holy Spirit, help me to pray at all times today. Keep me watchful and faithful, and put on my heart the people who need prayer. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy150', 150, '1 Corinthians 2:12', 'Now we have received, not the spirit of the world, but the spirit which is of God; that we might know the things that are freely given to us of God.', 'The Spirit of God helps us see and understand the good things God has freely given us in Christ.', 'I have received the Spirit which is of God, so I can know the things freely given to me by God.', 'Father, open my eyes by Your Spirit to see all You have freely given me in Christ. Let me live today with a grateful and understanding heart. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy151', 151, 'Acts 4:31', 'And when they had prayed, the place was shaken where they were assembled together; and they were all filled with the Holy Ghost, and they spake the word of God with boldness.', 'When the early church prayed together, God filled them with the Spirit and gave them boldness to speak His word.', 'As I pray, I am filled with the Holy Ghost, and I speak the word of God with boldness.', 'Lord, as I pray today, fill me again with Your Holy Spirit. Give me gentle boldness to speak Your word wherever You send me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy152', 152, 'Job 28:28', 'And unto man he said, Behold, the fear of the LORD, that is wisdom; and to depart from evil is understanding.', 'Wisdom begins with honouring God and turning away from what is wrong. It is less about cleverness and more about reverence.', 'The fear of the Lord is wisdom, and departing from evil is understanding. I choose to honour God and walk in His wisdom today.', 'Lord, teach me the wisdom of reverence. Help me to honour You in every choice and to turn gently away from what is wrong. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy153', 153, 'Ephesians 2:10', 'For we are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus unto good works, which God hath before ordained that we should walk in them.', 'You are God''s handiwork, made in Christ for good works He prepared in advance. Your life has purpose.', 'I am God''s workmanship, created in Christ Jesus for good works, and I walk in the good works He prepared for me.', 'Father, thank You for making me with purpose. Open my eyes today to the good works You have prepared, and give me grace to walk in them. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy154', 154, 'Proverbs 12:25', 'Heaviness in the heart of man maketh it stoop: but a good word maketh it glad.', 'Worry weighs a heart down, but one good word can lift it. Your kind word today may be someone''s relief.', 'Heaviness will not bow me down; a good word makes my heart glad, and I will speak good words to others.', 'Father, lift the heaviness from my heart with Your good word. Help me to notice weary people today and to speak words that make them glad. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy155', 155, 'Colossians 3:23', 'And whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men;', 'Every task, seen or unseen, can be done wholeheartedly as service to the Lord. That turns ordinary work into worship.', 'Whatever I do today, I do it heartily as to the Lord, not just for people.', 'Lord, I offer You my work today. Help me to do it with my whole heart as service to You, whether anyone notices or not. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy156', 156, 'Proverbs 16:9', 'A man''s heart deviseth his way: but the LORD directeth his steps.', 'Make your plans, but hold them with open hands. The Lord directs your steps along the way.', 'My heart makes plans, and the Lord directs my steps. I trust Him to guide each one.', 'Lord, I bring You my plans for today. Direct my steps, adjust my path where needed, and give me peace to follow Your leading. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy157', 157, 'Proverbs 2:6', 'For the LORD giveth wisdom: out of his mouth cometh knowledge and understanding.', 'True wisdom, knowledge and understanding come from God''s own mouth. His word is where we find them.', 'The Lord gives wisdom. From His mouth come knowledge and understanding, and I listen to His word.', 'Lord, You are the giver of wisdom. As I read and listen to Your word, fill me with knowledge and understanding for the day ahead. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy158', 158, 'Psalm 19:14', 'Let the words of my mouth, and the meditation of my heart, be acceptable in thy sight, O LORD, my strength, and my redeemer.', 'God cares about both our words and our inner thoughts. We can invite Him to make both pleasing to Him.', 'The words of my mouth and the meditation of my heart are offered to the Lord, my strength and my redeemer.', 'Lord, my strength and my redeemer, let the words of my mouth and the thoughts of my heart be acceptable in Your sight today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy159', 159, 'Philippians 1:6', 'Being confident of this very thing, that he which hath begun a good work in you will perform it until the day of Jesus Christ:', 'God does not abandon unfinished work. What He started in you, He is faithfully carrying to completion.', 'I am confident that He who began a good work in me will carry it on until the day of Jesus Christ.', 'Father, thank You that You finish what You start. On days I feel unfinished, remind me that You are still at work in me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy160', 160, 'Proverbs 22:29', 'Seest thou a man diligent in his business? he shall stand before kings; he shall not stand before mean men.', 'Faithful, skilful work is noticed. Diligence opens doors that shortcuts never can.', 'I am diligent in my work, and God can bring my faithful labour before people of influence.', 'Lord, help me to be skilful and diligent in my work today. Let my faithfulness honour You, and open the doors You choose for me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.');
INSERT INTO devotions (id, sort, reference, text, reflection, declaration, prayer) VALUES
 ('dy161', 161, 'Proverbs 19:21', 'There are many devices in a man''s heart; nevertheless the counsel of the LORD, that shall stand.', 'We make many plans, and that is good. But it is the Lord''s purpose that stands, so we can hold our plans with trust.', 'My heart has many plans, but the counsel of the Lord will stand, and I trust His purpose over my life.', 'Lord, I bring You all my plans and ideas. Let Your counsel stand in my life, and give me peace when Your purpose differs from mine. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy162', 162, 'Proverbs 16:24', 'Pleasant words are as an honeycomb, sweet to the soul, and health to the bones.', 'Kind words are like honey. They sweeten the soul and bring healing to people who are tired or hurting.', 'My words are pleasant like honeycomb, bringing sweetness to souls and health to the bones.', 'Lord, let my words today be sweet and life-giving. Help me to encourage someone who is weary and to speak kindly at home and at work. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy163', 163, 'Proverbs 4:7', 'Wisdom is the principal thing; therefore get wisdom: and with all thy getting get understanding.', 'Of all the things we chase, wisdom is the most important. Seek understanding above everything else.', 'Wisdom is the principal thing, so I seek wisdom, and with all my getting I get understanding.', 'Father, make wisdom my first pursuit. Above every other goal, give me a heart that seeks understanding from You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy164', 164, 'Romans 12:2', 'And be not conformed to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what is that good, and acceptable, and perfect, will of God.', 'God changes us from the inside by renewing our minds, so we can recognise His good and perfect will.', 'I am not conformed to this world; I am transformed by the renewing of my mind, and I discern God''s good, acceptable and perfect will.', 'Lord, renew my mind today. Shape my thinking by Your truth instead of the world''s pressure, and help me to know and follow Your good will. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy165', 165, 'Galatians 6:9', 'And let us not be weary in well doing: for in due season we shall reap, if we faint not.', 'Doing good can feel tiring when results seem slow. Keep going; a harvest comes in God''s season.', 'I will not grow weary in doing good. In due season I will reap, and I will not give up.', 'Father, when I feel tired of doing right, refresh my strength. Help me to keep sowing good, trusting that Your harvest will come in due season. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy166', 166, 'Proverbs 18:21', 'Death and life are in the power of the tongue: and they that love it shall eat the fruit thereof.', 'Our words carry weight. They can build life or tear down, so speak with care and grace.', 'Life and death are in the power of the tongue, and I choose to speak words of life today.', 'Lord, help me to understand the power of my words. Let me speak life over my family, my work and myself today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy167', 167, 'Luke 16:10', 'He that is faithful in that which is least is faithful also in much: and he that is unjust in the least is unjust also in much.', 'Faithfulness in small, unseen tasks is not wasted. It is how God grows trustworthy people for greater things.', 'I am faithful in little things, and by God''s grace I grow faithful in much.', 'Lord Jesus, help me to be faithful in the small tasks in front of me today. Let my faithfulness in little things honour You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy168', 168, '2 Timothy 1:9', 'Who hath saved us, and called us with an holy calling, not according to our works, but according to his own purpose and grace, which was given us in Christ Jesus before the world began,', 'Your calling was not earned; it flows from God''s purpose and grace, given in Christ before time began.', 'God has saved me and called me with a holy calling, not because of my works but by His own purpose and grace in Christ.', 'Father, thank You for saving me and calling me by grace. Help me to live today with the confidence that Your purpose is over my life. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy169', 169, 'Colossians 4:6', 'Let your speech be alway with grace, seasoned with salt, that ye may know how ye ought to answer every man.', 'Gracious words, seasoned with salt, are kind yet meaningful. They help us know how to answer each person well.', 'My speech is always with grace, seasoned with salt, and I know how to answer each person.', 'Lord, season my words with grace today. Give me wisdom to answer each person kindly and truthfully, in a way that honours You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy170', 170, 'Proverbs 24:3-4', 'Through wisdom is an house builded; and by understanding it is established: And by knowledge shall the chambers be filled with all precious and pleasant riches.', 'Strong homes and lives are built with wisdom, established by understanding, and filled through knowledge.', 'Through wisdom my house is built, by understanding it is established, and by knowledge its rooms are filled with precious and pleasant things.', 'Father, build my home and my life with Your wisdom. Establish us with understanding, and fill our rooms with what is precious and pleasant in Your sight. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy171', 171, 'Proverbs 15:23', 'A man hath joy by the answer of his mouth: and a word spoken in due season, how good is it!', 'A well-timed word brings joy to the one who speaks it and to the one who hears it.', 'I have joy in the answer of my mouth, and I speak words in due season.', 'Lord, give me good answers today and teach me the right timing for my words. Let what I say bring joy to others and to You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy172', 172, 'Ephesians 4:29', 'Let no corrupt communication proceed out of your mouth, but that which is good to the use of edifying, that it may minister grace unto the hearers.', 'Before speaking, ask: will this build up? Good words minister grace to everyone who hears them.', 'I let no corrupt words come out of my mouth, only what is good for building up, so my words minister grace to those who hear.', 'Father, fill my mouth with words that build up. Let everything I say today minister grace to those who hear it. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy173', 173, '1 Corinthians 15:58', 'Therefore, my beloved brethren, be ye stedfast, unmoveable, always abounding in the work of the Lord, forasmuch as ye know that your labour is not in vain in the Lord.', 'Work done for the Lord is never wasted. Stay steady; your labour in Him is not in vain.', 'I am steadfast and unmovable, always abounding in the work of the Lord, knowing my labour in the Lord is not in vain.', 'Lord, keep me steady and faithful today. When I wonder if my efforts matter, remind me that nothing done for You is ever in vain. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy174', 174, 'Proverbs 11:14', 'Where no counsel is, the people fall: but in the multitude of counsellors there is safety.', 'Wise decisions are rarely made alone. Seeking godly counsel brings safety and clarity.', 'I do not walk alone in my decisions. I seek wise counsel, and in many counsellors there is safety.', 'Father, lead me to wise and godly counsellors. Give me a humble heart to listen and good judgment to decide well. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy175', 175, 'James 3:17', 'But the wisdom that is from above is first pure, then peaceable, gentle, and easy to be intreated, full of mercy and good fruits, without partiality, and without hypocrisy.', 'Wisdom from God is pure, peaceable and gentle. It shows up in mercy, good fruit and sincerity.', 'The wisdom from above fills me: pure, peaceable, gentle, open to reason, full of mercy and good fruits, without partiality or hypocrisy.', 'Lord, fill me with the wisdom that comes from above. Make me peaceable, gentle and merciful, and let my life bear good fruit today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy176', 176, 'Ecclesiastes 9:10', 'Whatsoever thy hand findeth to do, do it with thy might; for there is no work, nor device, nor knowledge, nor wisdom, in the grave, whither thou goest.', 'Life is short and today''s opportunities are real. Whatever your hand finds to do, give it your full strength.', 'Whatever my hand finds to do today, I do it with my might.', 'Lord, help me to give my best to the tasks before me today. Let me work with energy and joy while I have the opportunity. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy177', 177, 'Psalm 141:3', 'Set a watch, O LORD, before my mouth; keep the door of my lips.', 'Sometimes the wisest prayer is simple: Lord, guard my mouth. He can help us hold back words we would regret.', 'The Lord sets a watch before my mouth and keeps the door of my lips.', 'Lord, set a guard over my mouth today. Keep the door of my lips, and help me to speak only what pleases You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy178', 178, 'Proverbs 4:25-26', 'Let thine eyes look right on, and let thine eyelids look straight before thee. Ponder the path of thy feet, and let all thy ways be established.', 'Good decisions need focus. Keep your eyes forward, think through your path, and let God establish your ways.', 'I keep my eyes looking straight ahead. I ponder the path of my feet, and my ways are established.', 'Father, help me to stay focused and not be distracted. Give me wisdom to think carefully about my path and establish my steps. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy179', 179, 'Luke 2:52', 'And Jesus increased in wisdom and stature, and in favour with God and man.', 'Even Jesus grew step by step in wisdom and stature. Growth takes time, and God is patient with your growing.', 'Like Jesus, I can grow in wisdom and stature and in favour with God and people, one day at a time.', 'Father, as Jesus grew in wisdom and favour, help me to grow too. Be patient with me as I learn, and shape me day by day. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy180', 180, 'Proverbs 25:11', 'A word fitly spoken is like apples of gold in pictures of silver.', 'The right word at the right time is beautiful and precious. Ask God for timing as well as words.', 'I speak words fitly spoken, at the right time, like apples of gold in settings of silver.', 'Lord, give me the right words at the right moment today. Let my speech be beautiful and fitting, a blessing to those who hear. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy181', 181, 'Psalm 90:17', 'And let the beauty of the LORD our God be upon us: and establish thou the work of our hands upon us; yea, the work of our hands establish thou it.', 'We can ask God to let His beauty rest on us and to establish the work of our hands so it lasts.', 'The beauty of the Lord my God is upon me, and He establishes the work of my hands.', 'Lord our God, let Your beauty rest upon me. Establish the work of my hands, and make what I build today fruitful and lasting. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy182', 182, 'James 1:2-4', 'My brethren, count it all joy when ye fall into divers temptations; Knowing this, that the trying of your faith worketh patience. But let patience have her perfect work, that ye may be perfect and entire, wanting nothing.', 'Trials are not wasted. God uses the testing of your faith to grow patience in you, shaping you into someone whole and complete.', 'I choose joy in this season, because the testing of my faith is working patience in me, and God is making me whole.', 'Father, I don’t always feel joyful in hard times, but I trust You are at work. Let patience finish its work in me until I lack nothing. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy183', 183, 'James 1:12', 'Blessed is the man that endureth temptation: for when he is tried, he shall receive the crown of life, which the Lord hath promised to them that love him.', 'Enduring a hard season is not a sign of failure. God sees those who keep loving Him through trials, and He has promised them the crown of life.', 'I endure through this trial, and because I love the Lord, I shall receive the crown of life He has promised.', 'Lord, when I feel tested, keep my heart loving You. Help me endure one day at a time, holding on to the crown of life You have promised. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy184', 184, 'Hebrews 10:23', 'Let us hold fast the profession of our faith without wavering; (for he is faithful that promised;)', 'Keep holding on to what you believe. Your grip may feel weak, but the One who made the promise is completely faithful.', 'I hold fast to my faith without wavering, because the God who promised me is faithful.', 'Faithful God, when I feel like letting go, remind me that You have never broken a promise. Steady my heart and help me hold on to You today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy185', 185, 'Psalm 36:5', 'Thy mercy, O LORD, is in the heavens; and thy faithfulness reacheth unto the clouds.', 'God’s mercy and faithfulness are bigger than any problem you face. They reach as high as the heavens and the clouds.', 'The Lord’s mercy toward me reaches to the heavens, and His faithfulness reaches to the clouds.', 'Father, lift my eyes above my troubles to the greatness of Your mercy. Thank You that Your faithfulness toward me is higher than the clouds. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy186', 186, 'Psalm 27:13-14', 'I had fainted, unless I had believed to see the goodness of the LORD in the land of the living. Wait on the LORD: be of good courage, and he shall strengthen thine heart: wait, I say, on the LORD.', 'David held on by believing he would see God’s goodness in this life. Wait on the Lord with courage; He will strengthen your heart.', 'I believe I will see the goodness of the Lord in the land of the living. I wait on Him with courage, and He strengthens my heart.', 'Lord, when I feel faint, help me keep believing I will see Your goodness. Give me courage while I wait, and strengthen my heart today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy187', 187, 'Isaiah 43:2', 'When thou passest through the waters, I will be with thee; and through the rivers, they shall not overflow thee: when thou walkest through the fire, thou shalt not be burned; neither shall the flame kindle upon thee.', 'God does not promise a life without deep waters or fire, but He promises to be with you in them, and they will not destroy you.', 'When I pass through the waters, God is with me. The rivers will not overflow me, and the fire will not burn me.', 'Father, thank You that I never walk through trouble alone. Be near me in every flood and fire I face, and keep me safe in Your hands. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy188', 188, '2 Corinthians 4:16-17', 'For which cause we faint not; but though our outward man perish, yet the inward man is renewed day by day. For our light affliction, which is but for a moment, worketh for us a far more exceeding and eternal weight of glory;', 'Your body may be tired, but God is renewing your inner life day by day. Today’s trouble is temporary and is working toward lasting glory.', 'I will not lose heart. My inner self is being renewed day by day, and my light affliction is working an eternal weight of glory for me.', 'Lord, renew me on the inside today. When my troubles feel heavy, help me see them in the light of eternity and the glory You are preparing. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy189', 189, 'Psalm 40:1-2', 'I waited patiently for the LORD; and he inclined unto me, and heard my cry. He brought me up also out of an horrible pit, out of the miry clay, and set my feet upon a rock, and established my goings.', 'Patient waiting is not wasted. God hears the cry of the one who waits, lifts them from the pit, and sets their feet on solid rock.', 'I wait patiently for the Lord, and He hears my cry. He lifts me out of the miry clay and sets my feet upon a rock.', 'Father, I bring You my cry today. Lift me from every pit and set my feet on the rock. Establish my steps as I wait on You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy190', 190, 'Romans 12:12', 'Rejoicing in hope; patient in tribulation; continuing instant in prayer;', 'Three simple habits for hard seasons: keep rejoicing in hope, stay patient in trouble, and keep praying without giving up.', 'I rejoice in hope, I stay patient in tribulation, and I keep on praying.', 'Lord, fill me with hope that makes me glad. Give me patience in what I am facing, and keep me close to You in prayer all day long. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy191', 191, '1 Peter 5:10', 'But the God of all grace, who hath called us unto his eternal glory by Christ Jesus, after that ye have suffered a while, make you perfect, stablish, strengthen, settle you.', 'Suffering is not the end of your story. After a while, the God of all grace will restore you, make you strong, firm and settled.', 'The God of all grace has called me to His eternal glory. After this season, He will perfect, establish, strengthen and settle me.', 'God of all grace, You see what I have walked through. Restore me, strengthen me and settle my heart in You, for You have called me to Your glory. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy192', 192, 'Hebrews 12:1', 'Wherefore seeing we also are compassed about with so great a cloud of witnesses, let us lay aside every weight, and the sin which doth so easily beset us, and let us run with patience the race that is set before us,', 'Many have run this race before you and finished well. Lay down what weighs you down and keep running at a steady, patient pace.', 'I lay aside every weight and the sin that entangles me, and I run with patience the race set before me.', 'Father, help me let go of what slows me down. Give me endurance for my race today, and remind me I am surrounded by those who finished faithfully. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy193', 193, 'Hebrews 10:35-36', 'Cast not away therefore your confidence, which hath great recompence of reward. For ye have need of patience, that, after ye have done the will of God, ye might receive the promise.', 'Don’t throw away your confidence in God just because the wait is long. Patience helps you keep doing His will until you receive what He promised.', 'I will not cast away my confidence in God. I have patience, and after doing His will, I shall receive the promise.', 'Father, guard my confidence in You when waiting feels long. Give me patience to keep doing Your will, trusting You to keep Your promise. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy194', 194, 'James 5:7-8', 'Be patient therefore, brethren, unto the coming of the Lord. Behold, the husbandman waiteth for the precious fruit of the earth, and hath long patience for it, until he receive the early and latter rain. Be ye also patient; stablish your hearts: for the coming of the Lord draweth nigh.', 'A farmer waits patiently for the rain and the crop. Like him, steady your heart and wait with hope, for the Lord’s coming is near.', 'I am patient like the farmer who waits for the rain. I establish my heart, because the coming of the Lord draws near.', 'Lord, teach me the patience of the farmer. Steady my heart while I wait, and fill me with hope as I look forward to Your coming. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy195', 195, 'Psalm 30:5', 'For his anger endureth but a moment; in his favour is life: weeping may endure for a night, but joy cometh in the morning.', 'Tears may last through the night, but they are not the end. In God’s favour there is life, and joy comes in the morning.', 'Weeping may last for a night, but joy comes in the morning. In God’s favour there is life for me.', 'Father, You see every tear I have cried. Carry me through the night and let me wake to Your joy. Thank You that Your favour brings life. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy196', 196, 'Habakkuk 3:17-18', 'Although the fig tree shall not blossom, neither shall fruit be in the vines; the labour of the olive shall fail, and the fields shall yield no meat; the flock shall be cut off from the fold, and there shall be no herd in the stalls: Yet I will rejoice in the LORD, I will joy in the God of my salvation.', 'Even when everything around him failed, Habakkuk chose to rejoice in God. Your joy can rest in who God is, not only in what you see.', 'Even when things fail around me, I will rejoice in the Lord. I will be joyful in the God of my salvation.', 'Lord, when my fields look empty, be my joy. I choose to rejoice in You, the God who saves me, whatever I see around me today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy197', 197, 'Nahum 1:7', 'The LORD is good, a strong hold in the day of trouble; and he knoweth them that trust in him.', 'On your hardest day, God is good and He is a strong place to hide. He knows you personally when you trust Him.', 'The Lord is good. He is my stronghold in the day of trouble, and He knows me because I trust in Him.', 'Lord, You are good, even when my day is hard. Be my stronghold today, and thank You that You know me and hold me close. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy198', 198, '1 Peter 1:6-7', 'Wherein ye greatly rejoice, though now for a season, if need be, ye are in heaviness through manifold temptations: That the trial of your faith, being much more precious than of gold that perisheth, though it be tried with fire, might be found unto praise and honour and glory at the appearing of Jesus Christ:', 'Heavy seasons can come, but they are only for a season. Tested faith is more precious than gold and will bring praise to Jesus.', 'Though I am in heaviness for a season, I rejoice. My tested faith is more precious than gold and will bring praise to Jesus.', 'Lord, You know the heaviness I feel. Help me rejoice in You through this season, and let my tested faith bring honour to Jesus. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy199', 199, 'Psalm 46:1-2', 'God is our refuge and strength, a very present help in trouble. Therefore will not we fear, though the earth be removed, and though the mountains be carried into the midst of the sea;', 'When everything seems to shake, God stays your safe place and your strength. He is not far away; He is present help right now.', 'God is my refuge and strength, a very present help in trouble. Therefore I will not fear, even if the earth gives way.', 'Father, be my refuge today. When things around me shake, hold me steady and quiet my fears with Your nearness. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy200', 200, 'Isaiah 41:10', 'Fear thou not; for I am with thee: be not dismayed; for I am thy God: I will strengthen thee; yea, I will help thee; yea, I will uphold thee with the right hand of my righteousness.', 'God answers fear with His presence. He promises to strengthen you, help you and hold you up with His righteous right hand.', 'I will not fear, for God is with me. He strengthens me, He helps me, and He upholds me with His righteous right hand.', 'Lord, when fear rises, remind me that You are my God and You are with me. Strengthen me, help me and hold me up today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.');
INSERT INTO devotions (id, sort, reference, text, reflection, declaration, prayer) VALUES
 ('dy201', 201, 'Psalm 28:7', 'The LORD is my strength and my shield; my heart trusted in him, and I am helped: therefore my heart greatly rejoiceth; and with my song will I praise him.', 'When your strength runs low, the Lord becomes your strength and shield. Trust Him, and you will find help and a song again.', 'The Lord is my strength and my shield. My heart trusts in Him, and I am helped, so I will praise Him with my song.', 'Lord, be my strength and my shield today. I put my trust in You; help me, and fill my heart with joy and a song of praise. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy202', 202, 'Psalm 71:20', 'Thou, which hast shewed me great and sore troubles, shalt quicken me again, and shalt bring me up again from the depths of the earth.', 'The psalmist had seen great troubles, yet he trusted God to revive him. The God who saw you through the depths can bring you up again.', 'The God who has seen me through great troubles will revive me again and bring me up again from the depths.', 'Father, You know the troubles I have walked through. Revive me again, lift me from low places, and renew my hope in You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy203', 203, 'Psalm 34:18-19', 'The LORD is nigh unto them that are of a broken heart; and saveth such as be of a contrite spirit. Many are the afflictions of the righteous: but the LORD delivereth him out of them all.', 'God draws especially close to the brokenhearted. Troubles may be many, but the Lord brings His people through them all.', 'The Lord is near to me when my heart is broken. Though afflictions may be many, the Lord delivers me out of them all.', 'Lord, draw near to my heart today. Where I am hurting, be close; where I am troubled, deliver me, as You have promised. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy204', 204, 'Psalm 57:1', 'Be merciful unto me, O God, be merciful unto me: for my soul trusteth in thee: yea, in the shadow of thy wings will I make my refuge, until these calamities be overpast.', 'Faith runs to God when calamities come. You can hide under the shadow of His wings until the storm passes.', 'My soul trusts in God. In the shadow of His wings I make my refuge until these calamities are past.', 'Merciful God, I run to You today. Cover me in the shadow of Your wings and keep me safe until this storm has passed. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy205', 205, '1 Corinthians 10:13', 'There hath no temptation taken you but such as is common to man: but God is faithful, who will not suffer you to be tempted above that ye are able; but will with the temptation also make a way to escape, that ye may be able to bear it.', 'Your struggle is not unusual, and you are not alone. God is faithful; He will not let it go beyond what you can bear, and He provides a way through.', 'God is faithful. He will not let me be tempted beyond what I can bear, and He makes a way of escape for me.', 'Faithful God, when temptation presses on me, show me the way of escape You have made. Give me strength to take it and to stand. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy206', 206, 'Psalm 42:11', 'Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him, who is the health of my countenance, and my God.', 'It’s okay to be honest about a heavy soul. Speak hope to yourself: you will yet praise God again.', 'When my soul is cast down, I choose to hope in God. I shall yet praise Him, the health of my countenance and my God.', 'Lord, You know when my soul feels low. Lift my eyes to You, fill me with hope, and give me a song of praise again. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy207', 207, 'Lamentations 3:25-26', 'The LORD is good unto them that wait for him, to the soul that seeketh him. It is good that a man should both hope and quietly wait for the salvation of the LORD.', 'Waiting quietly on God is not passive; it is trust. The Lord is good to those who wait for Him and seek Him.', 'The Lord is good to me as I wait for Him and seek Him. I hope and quietly wait for His salvation.', 'Father, quiet my restless heart. Help me seek You and wait for You with hope, trusting that You are good. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy208', 208, 'Hebrews 6:19', 'Which hope we have as an anchor of the soul, both sure and stedfast, and which entereth into that within the veil;', 'Storms will come, but hope in God is an anchor that holds. It is sure and steady, fastened in His very presence.', 'My hope in God is an anchor for my soul, sure and steadfast, and it holds me firm in every storm.', 'Lord, anchor my soul in You today. When the winds blow, keep me steady in the sure hope I have in Jesus. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy209', 209, 'Isaiah 54:10', 'For the mountains shall depart, and the hills be removed; but my kindness shall not depart from thee, neither shall the covenant of my peace be removed, saith the LORD that hath mercy on thee.', 'Even mountains can move, but God’s kindness toward you will not. His covenant of peace stands firm.', 'Though mountains depart and hills be removed, God’s kindness shall not depart from me, and His covenant of peace shall not be removed.', 'Merciful Father, thank You that Your kindness toward me is more lasting than the mountains. Let Your peace settle my heart today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy210', 210, '2 Timothy 4:7', 'I have fought a good fight, I have finished my course, I have kept the faith:', 'Paul looked back on a life of faithful endurance. One day at a time, you too can keep the faith and finish your course well.', 'By God’s grace, I will fight the good fight, finish my course and keep the faith.', 'Lord, help me stay faithful today and every day. Give me strength to keep going, and let me finish my course holding on to You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy211', 211, 'Romans 8:18', 'For I reckon that the sufferings of this present time are not worthy to be compared with the glory which shall be revealed in us.', 'Present pain is real, but it is small compared with the glory God will reveal in His people.', 'The sufferings of this present time are not worthy to be compared with the glory that shall be revealed in me.', 'Father, lift my eyes beyond today’s struggles. Remind me of the glory You will reveal, and give me hope that outweighs my pain. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy212', 212, 'Psalm 138:8', 'The LORD will perfect that which concerneth me: thy mercy, O LORD, endureth for ever: forsake not the works of thine own hands.', 'God finishes what He starts. He will complete what concerns you, and His mercy toward you lasts forever.', 'The Lord will perfect that which concerns me. His mercy endures forever, and He will not abandon the work of His hands.', 'Lord, I place everything that concerns me in Your hands. Complete Your good work in my life, for Your mercy endures forever. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy213', 213, 'Psalm 23:2-3', 'He maketh me to lie down in green pastures: he leadeth me beside the still waters. He restoreth my soul: he leadeth me in the paths of righteousness for his name''s sake.', 'Your Shepherd knows when you need to lie down. He leads you to quiet places, restores your soul and guides your steps.', 'The Lord makes me lie down in green pastures and leads me beside still waters. He restores my soul and leads me in right paths.', 'Good Shepherd, lead me to rest today. Restore my weary soul beside Your still waters, and guide my steps in paths that honour Your name. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy214', 214, 'Matthew 6:26', 'Behold the fowls of the air: for they sow not, neither do they reap, nor gather into barns; yet your heavenly Father feedeth them. Are ye not much better than they?', 'The birds don’t store up barns, yet your Father feeds them. You are worth far more to Him than they are.', 'My heavenly Father feeds the birds of the air, and I am of much more value to Him than they are.', 'Father, when I worry about tomorrow, remind me of the birds You feed. Help me trust that I am precious to You and that You care for me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy215', 215, 'Hebrews 4:9-10', 'There remaineth therefore a rest to the people of God. For he that is entered into his rest, he also hath ceased from his own works, as God did from his.', 'God has a rest for His people. You can stop striving to earn His love and rest in what He has already done.', 'A rest remains for me as one of God’s people. I enter His rest and cease from my own striving.', 'Father, thank You for the rest You have prepared for me. Help me stop striving and rest in Your finished work and faithful love. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy216', 216, 'Philippians 4:19', 'But my God shall supply all your need according to his riches in glory by Christ Jesus.', 'Paul wrote this to friends who had generously cared for him. The God who sees your needs supplies them from His riches in Christ.', 'My God shall supply all my need according to His riches in glory by Christ Jesus.', 'Father, You know every need I carry today. I trust You to supply them from Your riches in Christ, and I thank You in advance for Your care. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy217', 217, 'Psalm 55:22', 'Cast thy burden upon the LORD, and he shall sustain thee: he shall never suffer the righteous to be moved.', 'You were never meant to carry your burdens alone. Hand them to the Lord; He will hold you up and keep you steady.', 'I cast my burden upon the Lord, and He sustains me. He will not let me be moved.', 'Lord, I place my burdens in Your hands today. Sustain me and keep me steady, for You are faithful to hold me up. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy218', 218, 'Psalm 37:25', 'I have been young, and now am old; yet have I not seen the righteous forsaken, nor his seed begging bread.', 'After a lifetime of watching, David testified that God does not abandon the righteous. His care reaches across generations.', 'The Lord does not forsake His people. He has been faithful through every season, and He will be faithful to me and my children.', 'Faithful Father, thank You for Your care through all my years. Keep me and my family in Your faithful hands, today and in the years to come. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy219', 219, 'Hebrews 13:5', 'Let your conversation be without covetousness; and be content with such things as ye have: for he hath said, I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee.', 'Contentment grows from knowing God is with you. Whatever you have or lack, He has promised never to leave you.', 'I am content with what I have, for God has said, I will never leave you nor forsake you.', 'Lord, free my heart from always wanting more. Teach me contentment in Your constant presence, for You will never leave me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy220', 220, 'Philippians 4:11-12', 'Not that I speak in respect of want: for I have learned, in whatsoever state I am, therewith to be content. I know both how to be abased, and I know how to abound: every where and in all things I am instructed both to be full and to be hungry, both to abound and to suffer need.', 'Contentment is learned, not instant. Paul learned it in both plenty and need, and God can teach you too.', 'I am learning to be content in every state, whether I have little or much, full or hungry.', 'Father, teach me the secret of contentment. In plenty and in need, keep my heart settled in You rather than in my circumstances. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy221', 221, '1 Timothy 6:6-7', 'But godliness with contentment is great gain. For we brought nothing into this world, and it is certain we can carry nothing out.', 'Real gain is a godly life with a content heart. We brought nothing in and take nothing out, so hold things lightly.', 'Godliness with contentment is great gain to me. I hold earthly things lightly, for I brought nothing into this world.', 'Lord, help me value what truly lasts. Give me a godly and content heart, and loosen my grip on things I cannot keep. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy222', 222, 'Psalm 107:8-9', 'Oh that men would praise the LORD for his goodness, and for his wonderful works to the children of men! For he satisfieth the longing soul, and filleth the hungry soul with goodness.', 'God sees the deep longings of your soul. He satisfies the thirsty and fills the hungry with His goodness; that is worth praising Him for.', 'I praise the Lord for His goodness and wonderful works. He satisfies my longing soul and fills me with goodness.', 'Father, thank You for Your goodness and wonderful works. Satisfy the longings of my soul today, and fill me with Your goodness. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy223', 223, '1 Thessalonians 5:18', 'In every thing give thanks: for this is the will of God in Christ Jesus concerning you.', 'Not thanks for every bad thing, but thanks in every situation. Gratitude keeps your heart open to God wherever you are.', 'In everything I give thanks, for this is God’s will for me in Christ Jesus.', 'Lord, open my eyes to the gifts around me. In every situation today, help me find a reason to thank You, because You are still good. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy224', 224, 'Psalm 103:2-4', 'Bless the LORD, O my soul, and forget not all his benefits: Who forgiveth all thine iniquities; who healeth all thy diseases; Who redeemeth thy life from destruction; who crowneth thee with lovingkindness and tender mercies;', 'Take time to remember what God has done. He forgives, heals, redeems and crowns you with lovingkindness and tender mercies.', 'I bless the Lord and forget not His benefits. He forgives me, heals me, redeems my life and crowns me with lovingkindness and tender mercies.', 'Father, I bless You with my whole heart. Thank You for forgiveness, healing and redemption. Help me never forget Your kindness to me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy225', 225, 'Proverbs 11:25', 'The liberal soul shall be made fat: and he that watereth shall be watered also himself.', 'Generous people are refreshed. When you pour out kindness on others, God makes sure you are watered too.', 'I am generous toward others, and as I water others, I too shall be watered.', 'Lord, give me a generous spirit today. Show me someone I can refresh, and let me pour out kindness freely, trusting You to refresh me too. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy226', 226, 'Acts 20:35', 'I have shewed you all things, how that so labouring ye ought to support the weak, and to remember the words of the Lord Jesus, how he said, It is more blessed to give than to receive.', 'Jesus taught that giving brings more blessing than receiving. Helping the weak is a joy, not just a duty.', 'I support the weak and remember the words of Jesus: it is more blessed to give than to receive.', 'Jesus, make me quick to notice those who are struggling. Give me joy in helping them, and let Your words shape how I live today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy227', 227, '2 Corinthians 9:8', 'And God is able to make all grace abound toward you; that ye, always having all sufficiency in all things, may abound to every good work:', 'God can pour grace on you so that you have what you need for every good work He places before you.', 'God is able to make all grace abound toward me, so that I have sufficiency in all things for every good work.', 'Father, let Your grace overflow in my life. Give me enough of what I need, and more than enough to do the good works You have prepared for me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy228', 228, 'Psalm 127:2', 'It is vain for you to rise up early, to sit up late, to eat the bread of sorrows: for so he giveth his beloved sleep.', 'Endless anxious toil is not God’s plan for you. He loves you, and rest is one of His gifts to His beloved.', 'I am God’s beloved, and He gives me sleep. I do not have to toil in anxiety.', 'Father, release me from anxious striving. Help me work faithfully, then lay my burdens down and receive the rest You give to those You love. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy229', 229, 'Exodus 33:14', 'And he said, My presence shall go with thee, and I will give thee rest.', 'God promised Moses His presence and His rest. Wherever today takes you, He goes with you and gives you rest.', 'God’s presence goes with me, and He gives me rest.', 'Lord, go with me into this day. Let Your presence be my peace and my rest in every task and every conversation. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy230', 230, 'Psalm 41:1', 'Blessed is he that considereth the poor: the LORD will deliver him in time of trouble.', 'God notices when you notice the poor. Caring for those in need is close to His heart, and He cares for you in your own trouble.', 'I consider the poor and care for those in need, and the Lord delivers me in time of trouble.', 'Father, give me eyes to see the poor and a heart to help them. Thank You that You are my deliverer in times of trouble. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy231', 231, 'Psalm 145:15-16', 'The eyes of all wait upon thee; and thou givest them their meat in due season. Thou openest thine hand, and satisfiest the desire of every living thing.', 'All creation looks to God, and He feeds it in due season. His open hand satisfies every living thing, including you.', 'I look to the Lord, and He gives me what I need in due season. He opens His hand and satisfies me.', 'Lord, my eyes wait on You today. Thank You for Your open hand and Your perfect timing. Satisfy me with Your goodness. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy232', 232, 'Psalm 68:19', 'Blessed be the Lord, who daily loadeth us with benefits, even the God of our salvation. Selah.', 'God doesn’t provide only once in a while. Every single day He loads you with benefits; look for them today.', 'Blessed be the Lord, who daily loads me with benefits. He is the God of my salvation.', 'Lord, thank You for the benefits You pour on me every day. Open my eyes to Your daily goodness and fill my heart with praise. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy233', 233, 'Psalm 4:8', 'I will both lay me down in peace, and sleep: for thou, LORD, only makest me dwell in safety.', 'You can lie down in peace tonight. Safety does not ultimately come from you but from the Lord who watches over you.', 'I will lie down in peace and sleep, for the Lord alone makes me dwell in safety.', 'Lord, quiet my mind tonight. Watch over me and my home, and let me sleep in peace, knowing You keep me safe. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy234', 234, 'Hebrews 13:16', 'But to do good and to communicate forget not: for with such sacrifices God is well pleased.', 'Doing good and sharing with others is worship that pleases God. Small acts of kindness matter to Him.', 'I do not forget to do good and to share with others, for God is well pleased with such sacrifices.', 'Lord, show me where I can do good and share today. Let my kindness to others be an offering that pleases You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy235', 235, 'Psalm 136:1', 'O give thanks unto the LORD; for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever.', 'The simplest reason to give thanks never changes: God is good, and His mercy lasts forever.', 'I give thanks to the Lord, for He is good, and His mercy endures forever.', 'Father, I thank You because You are good. Your mercy has carried me until now, and it will carry me forever. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy236', 236, 'Genesis 22:14', 'And Abraham called the name of that place Jehovahjireh: as it is said to this day, In the mount of the LORD it shall be seen.', 'On the mountain Abraham discovered God as the Lord who provides. He sees ahead and makes provision in His time.', 'The Lord is my Jehovah Jireh. On the mount of the Lord it shall be seen; He sees and provides.', 'Jehovah Jireh, thank You that You see what I need before I do. Help me trust You on the mountain, knowing You will provide. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy237', 237, 'Proverbs 19:17', 'He that hath pity upon the poor lendeth unto the LORD; and that which he hath given will he pay him again.', 'Kindness to the poor is so precious to God that He counts it as a loan to Himself, and He will repay it.', 'When I show kindness to the poor, I lend to the Lord, and He will repay what I have given.', 'Lord, give me a heart of compassion for the poor. Open my eyes to those in need and my hands to help them, as unto You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy238', 238, 'Colossians 3:15', 'And let the peace of God rule in your hearts, to the which also ye are called in one body; and be ye thankful.', 'Let God’s peace be the referee in your heart today, and keep a thankful spirit alongside the people around you.', 'The peace of God rules in my heart, and I am thankful.', 'Lord, let Your peace rule my heart today. Calm every restless thought, and fill me with thankfulness for You and for the people You have given me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy239', 239, 'Psalm 34:10', 'The young lions do lack, and suffer hunger: but they that seek the LORD shall not want any good thing.', 'Even strong lions go hungry sometimes, but those who seek the Lord will not lack any good thing.', 'I seek the Lord, and I shall not lack any good thing.', 'Father, I seek You today above everything else. Thank You that You withhold no good thing from me, and help me trust Your goodness. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy240', 240, 'Mark 6:31', 'And he said unto them, Come ye yourselves apart into a desert place, and rest a while: for there were many coming and going, and they had no leisure so much as to eat.', 'Jesus noticed His busy disciples were too tired to eat, and He invited them to rest. He extends the same invitation to you.', 'Jesus invites me to come apart and rest a while, and I accept His invitation.', 'Jesus, thank You for caring about my weariness. Help me step away from the rush today, rest with You, and be refreshed. In Jesus'' name, Amen.');
INSERT INTO devotions (id, sort, reference, text, reflection, declaration, prayer) VALUES
 ('dy241', 241, 'James 1:17', 'Every good gift and every perfect gift is from above, and cometh down from the Father of lights, with whom is no variableness, neither shadow of turning.', 'Every good thing in your life is a gift from your unchanging Father. His goodness does not shift like shadows.', 'Every good and perfect gift in my life comes from my Father above, who never changes.', 'Father of lights, thank You for every good gift You have given me. Help me notice them and thank You, for You never change. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy242', 242, '1 Peter 4:9-10', 'Use hospitality one to another without grudging. As every man hath received the gift, even so minister the same one to another, as good stewards of the manifold grace of God.', 'Open your home and heart gladly. Whatever gift God has given you, use it to serve others as a steward of His grace.', 'I show hospitality without grudging, and I use the gift God gave me to serve others as a good steward of His grace.', 'Lord, make me warm and welcoming to others. Show me how to use my gifts to serve, and let Your grace flow through me today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy243', 243, 'Psalm 65:11', 'Thou crownest the year with thy goodness; and thy paths drop fatness.', 'God crowns the year with His goodness, and His paths overflow with abundance. Look back and see how He has provided.', 'God crowns my year with His goodness, and His paths overflow with abundance.', 'Father, thank You for the goodness You have shown me this year. Crown the rest of it with Your goodness, and help me walk in Your paths. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy244', 244, 'Ephesians 2:19', 'Now therefore ye are no more strangers and foreigners, but fellowcitizens with the saints, and of the household of God;', 'You are not an outsider looking in. In Christ you are a fellow citizen with God''s people and a member of His household.', 'I am no more a stranger or a foreigner. I am a fellow citizen with the saints and a member of the household of God.', 'Father, thank You for bringing me into Your family and giving me a place in Your household. Where I have felt like an outsider, help me live as one who truly belongs. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy245', 245, 'Colossians 2:10', 'And ye are complete in him, which is the head of all principality and power:', 'In Christ you are complete. You don''t need to chase something extra to be whole; He is the head over every power.', 'I am complete in Christ, who is the head of all principality and power.', 'Lord Jesus, thank You that I am complete in You. When I feel lacking, remind me that You are enough and that You are above every power. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy246', 246, '1 Peter 2:9', 'But ye are a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, an holy nation, a peculiar people; that ye should shew forth the praises of him who hath called you out of darkness into his marvellous light:', 'God calls you chosen, royal and His own. He brought you out of darkness so your life can shine with His praise.', 'I am chosen, a royal priesthood, God''s own special people. He called me out of darkness into His marvellous light, and I will show forth His praises.', 'Father, thank You for calling me out of darkness into Your marvellous light. Let my words and my life show forth Your praises today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy247', 247, 'John 1:12', 'But as many as received him, to them gave he power to become the sons of God, even to them that believe on his name:', 'Receiving Jesus changes who you are. To everyone who believes on His name, He gives the right to become a child of God.', 'I have received Jesus and believe on His name, and He has given me power to become a child of God.', 'Father, thank You for making me Your child through faith in Jesus. Help me live today with the security and joy of belonging to You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy248', 248, 'Ephesians 1:4', 'According as he hath chosen us in him before the foundation of the world, that we should be holy and without blame before him in love:', 'Long before you ever did anything right or wrong, God chose you in Christ to stand before Him holy and blameless in love.', 'God chose me in Christ before the foundation of the world. In Him I stand holy and without blame before Him in love.', 'Lord, it amazes me that You chose me before the world began. Help me rest in Your love and live as one You have made holy in Christ. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy249', 249, '1 John 3:2', 'Beloved, now are we the sons of God, and it doth not yet appear what we shall be: but we know that, when he shall appear, we shall be like him; for we shall see him as he is.', 'You are God''s child right now, not someday. And the best is still ahead: when Jesus appears, we shall be like Him.', 'Now I am a child of God. What I shall be has not yet appeared, but I know that when He appears I shall be like Him.', 'Father, thank You that I am already Your beloved child. Fill me with hope for what You are still doing in me, and keep my eyes on Jesus. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy250', 250, 'Colossians 3:3', 'For ye are dead, and your life is hid with Christ in God.', 'Your truest life is kept safe, hidden with Christ in God, where nothing and no one can snatch it away.', 'My life is hid with Christ in God. I am secure in Him today.', 'Father, thank You that my life is hidden with Christ in You. When I feel exposed or unsure, remind me that I am held safely in Your hands. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy251', 251, 'John 15:16', 'Ye have not chosen me, but I have chosen you, and ordained you, that ye should go and bring forth fruit, and that your fruit should remain: that whatsoever ye shall ask of the Father in my name, he may give it you.', 'Jesus chose you on purpose. He appointed you to bear fruit that lasts, and He invites you to ask the Father in His name.', 'Jesus chose me and ordained me to go and bring forth fruit that remains. I can ask the Father in His name.', 'Jesus, thank You for choosing me when I could not choose You first. Make my life fruitful in ways that last, and teach me to pray boldly in Your name. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy252', 252, 'Isaiah 43:1', 'But now thus saith the LORD that created thee, O Jacob, and he that formed thee, O Israel, Fear not: for I have redeemed thee, I have called thee by thy name; thou art mine.', 'The God who formed you says, fear not. He has redeemed you and called you by name. You belong to Him.', 'The Lord formed me and redeemed me. He has called me by my name, and I am His. I will not fear.', 'Lord, thank You for calling me by name and saying I am Yours. Quiet every fear in me today with the sound of Your voice. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy253', 253, 'Ephesians 1:5-6', 'Having predestinated us unto the adoption of children by Jesus Christ to himself, according to the good pleasure of his will, To the praise of the glory of his grace, wherein he hath made us accepted in the beloved.', 'Adoption was God''s joyful plan, not a reluctant decision. By His grace you are accepted in the Beloved, Jesus.', 'God adopted me as His child through Jesus Christ, according to the good pleasure of His will. By His grace I am accepted in the Beloved.', 'Father, thank You for choosing to adopt me and for the glory of Your grace. Let me rest today in knowing I am fully accepted in Jesus. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy254', 254, 'Titus 3:5', 'Not by works of righteousness which we have done, but according to his mercy he saved us, by the washing of regeneration, and renewing of the Holy Ghost;', 'Salvation was never your performance. God saved you by His mercy, washing you and renewing you by the Holy Spirit.', 'God saved me, not by works of righteousness I have done, but according to His mercy, by the washing of regeneration and renewing of the Holy Ghost.', 'Lord, thank You for saving me by Your mercy and not my merit. Renew me again today by Your Holy Spirit, and let me rest in Your kindness. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy255', 255, 'Romans 5:1', 'Therefore being justified by faith, we have peace with God through our Lord Jesus Christ:', 'You are made right with God by faith, not by effort. Because of Jesus, you have real peace with God right now.', 'I am justified by faith, and I have peace with God through my Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Lord, thank You that I am made right with You by faith in Jesus. Let Your peace settle my heart and quiet my striving today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy256', 256, '2 Corinthians 5:21', 'For he hath made him to be sin for us, who knew no sin; that we might be made the righteousness of God in him.', 'Jesus, who knew no sin, took our sin so that in Him we could be made the righteousness of God. What a trade.', 'Jesus was made sin for me, so that in Him I am made the righteousness of God.', 'Jesus, thank You for taking what I deserved so I could receive Your righteousness. Help me live today with the confidence of one made right in You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy257', 257, 'Philippians 3:9', 'And be found in him, not having mine own righteousness, which is of the law, but that which is through the faith of Christ, the righteousness which is of God by faith:', 'You don''t have to build your own righteousness. The righteousness that counts is a gift from God, received through faith in Christ.', 'I am found in Christ, not trusting in my own righteousness, but in the righteousness which is of God by faith.', 'Father, I let go of trying to earn Your approval. Thank You for the righteousness that comes through faith in Christ. Help me rest in it today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy258', 258, 'Romans 10:10', 'For with the heart man believeth unto righteousness; and with the mouth confession is made unto salvation.', 'Faith begins in the heart and finds its voice in the mouth. What you believe about Jesus is worth saying out loud.', 'With my heart I believe unto righteousness, and with my mouth I confess Jesus as Lord.', 'Lord, I believe in You with my heart, and I confess You with my mouth. Strengthen my faith and give me boldness to speak of You today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy259', 259, 'Galatians 5:1', 'Stand fast therefore in the liberty wherewith Christ hath made us free, and be not entangled again with the yoke of bondage.', 'Christ has set you free. Today, stand firm in that freedom and refuse to pick up the old yokes He already broke.', 'Christ has made me free. I stand fast in that liberty, and I will not be entangled again with the yoke of bondage.', 'Lord Jesus, thank You for the freedom You won for me. Give me strength to stand fast in it and to refuse every old chain that tries to return. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy260', 260, 'John 8:36', 'If the Son therefore shall make you free, ye shall be free indeed.', 'The freedom Jesus gives is not partial or pretend. When the Son sets you free, you are free indeed.', 'The Son has made me free, so I am free indeed.', 'Jesus, thank You that Your freedom is real and complete. Where I still feel bound, let me experience the freedom You have already given. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy261', 261, 'John 8:31-32', 'Then said Jesus to those Jews which believed on him, If ye continue in my word, then are ye my disciples indeed; And ye shall know the truth, and the truth shall make you free.', 'Freedom grows as you continue in Jesus'' word. His truth, known and lived, is what sets you free.', 'I continue in Jesus'' word; I am His disciple indeed. I shall know the truth, and the truth shall make me free.', 'Jesus, help me stay close to Your word today. Let Your truth replace every lie I have believed, and lead me into real freedom. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy262', 262, 'Colossians 1:13-14', 'Who hath delivered us from the power of darkness, and hath translated us into the kingdom of his dear Son: In whom we have redemption through his blood, even the forgiveness of sins:', 'God has already moved you out of darkness into the kingdom of His Son. Your redemption and forgiveness are settled in Jesus.', 'God has delivered me from the power of darkness and translated me into the kingdom of His dear Son. In Him I have redemption and forgiveness of sins.', 'Father, thank You for rescuing me from darkness and bringing me into Jesus'' kingdom. Help me live today as one who is forgiven and free. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy263', 263, 'Romans 8:15', 'For ye have not received the spirit of bondage again to fear; but ye have received the Spirit of adoption, whereby we cry, Abba, Father.', 'You did not receive a spirit that drives you back into fear. You received the Spirit of adoption, and you can call God ''Abba, Father.''', 'I have not received the spirit of bondage to fear. I have received the Spirit of adoption, and I cry, Abba, Father.', 'Abba, Father, thank You for adopting me as Your own. Replace every fearful thought with the settled trust of a loved child. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy264', 264, 'Colossians 3:10', 'And have put on the new man, which is renewed in knowledge after the image of him that created him:', 'You have put on the new self, and it keeps being renewed in knowledge, shaped more and more into the image of your Creator.', 'I have put on the new man, which is renewed in knowledge after the image of Him that created me.', 'Lord, keep renewing me in the knowledge of You. Shape my thoughts and my ways more and more into Your image today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy265', 265, 'Ephesians 4:23-24', 'And be renewed in the spirit of your mind; And that ye put on the new man, which after God is created in righteousness and true holiness.', 'Renewal is a daily putting on. Clothe yourself with the new self God created in righteousness and true holiness.', 'I am being renewed in the spirit of my mind. I put on the new man, created after God in righteousness and true holiness.', 'Father, renew the spirit of my mind today. Help me put on the new self You created in me and walk in righteousness and true holiness. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy266', 266, 'Philippians 4:8', 'Finally, brethren, whatsoever things are true, whatsoever things are honest, whatsoever things are just, whatsoever things are pure, whatsoever things are lovely, whatsoever things are of good report; if there be any virtue, and if there be any praise, think on these things.', 'What you dwell on shapes you. Today, choose to think on what is true, pure, lovely and praiseworthy.', 'I will think on whatsoever things are true, honest, just, pure, lovely and of good report.', 'Lord, guard my thoughts today. When my mind drifts toward worry or negativity, gently turn it back to what is true, lovely and good. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy267', 267, '2 Corinthians 10:5', 'Casting down imaginations, and every high thing that exalteth itself against the knowledge of God, and bringing into captivity every thought to the obedience of Christ;', 'You don''t have to believe every thought that comes. Bring each one to Christ and let His truth have the final word.', 'I cast down every imagination that exalts itself against the knowledge of God, and I bring every thought captive to the obedience of Christ.', 'Jesus, I bring my thoughts to You today. Help me recognise the lies that rise against Your truth and bring every thought under Your loving authority. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy268', 268, 'Colossians 3:2', 'Set your affection on things above, not on things on the earth.', 'Lift your gaze today. Setting your heart on things above helps you hold earthly things more lightly.', 'I set my affection on things above, not on things on the earth.', 'Father, lift my eyes to You today. Help me set my heart on what is eternal and hold the pressures of this world with open hands. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy269', 269, 'Psalm 94:19', 'In the multitude of my thoughts within me thy comforts delight my soul.', 'When your thoughts pile up and crowd in, God''s comforts can still bring delight to your soul.', 'In the multitude of my thoughts within me, God''s comforts delight my soul.', 'Lord, You see all the thoughts crowding my mind today. Meet me with Your comfort, and let it bring delight and rest to my soul. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy270', 270, '1 Corinthians 2:16', 'For who hath known the mind of the Lord, that he may instruct him? But we have the mind of Christ.', 'In Christ you are not left to your own understanding. By His Spirit you share in the mind of Christ.', 'I have the mind of Christ.', 'Holy Spirit, help me think Christ''s thoughts after Him today. Give me His wisdom, His compassion and His perspective in every decision I make. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy271', 271, '1 John 4:16', 'And we have known and believed the love that God hath to us. God is love; and he that dwelleth in love dwelleth in God, and God in him.', 'God''s love is not just something He does; God is love. Believing that love and dwelling in it means dwelling in Him.', 'I have known and believed the love that God has for me. God is love, and as I dwell in love, I dwell in God and God in me.', 'Father, I believe the love You have for me. Teach me to dwell in Your love today, and let it flow through me to others. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy272', 272, 'John 15:9', 'As the Father hath loved me, so have I loved you: continue ye in my love.', 'Jesus loves you the way the Father loves Him. His invitation today is simple: continue, remain, make your home in My love.', 'Jesus loves me as the Father has loved Him. I will continue in His love.', 'Jesus, thank You for loving me with the same love the Father has for You. Help me remain in Your love today and not wander from it. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy273', 273, 'Titus 3:7', 'That being justified by his grace, we should be made heirs according to the hope of eternal life.', 'Justified by grace, you are also an heir. Your future is secure in the hope of eternal life.', 'I am justified by His grace, and I am made an heir according to the hope of eternal life.', 'Father, thank You for justifying me by grace and making me an heir. Let the hope of eternal life steady my heart and lift my eyes today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy274', 274, 'Deuteronomy 31:6', 'Be strong and of a good courage, fear not, nor be afraid of them: for the LORD thy God, he it is that doth go with thee; he will not fail thee, nor forsake thee.', 'Courage doesn''t depend on how strong you feel. It rests on the fact that God goes with you and will not fail or forsake you.', 'I will be strong and of good courage. The Lord my God goes with me; He will not fail me nor forsake me.', 'Lord, thank You for going with me into this day. When I feel afraid, remind me that You will never fail me or forsake me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy275', 275, 'Psalm 27:1', 'The LORD is my light and my salvation; whom shall I fear? the LORD is the strength of my life; of whom shall I be afraid?', 'When God is your light, salvation and strength, fear loses its grip. You can face today knowing who stands with you.', 'The Lord is my light and my salvation; whom shall I fear? The Lord is the strength of my life.', 'Lord, be my light in every dark place and the strength of my life today. Teach my heart to answer fear with trust in You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy276', 276, 'Psalm 91:4', 'He shall cover thee with his feathers, and under his wings shalt thou trust: his truth shall be thy shield and buckler.', 'God''s protection is both tender and strong: sheltering wings over you and His faithful truth as your shield.', 'God covers me with His feathers, and under His wings I trust. His truth is my shield and buckler.', 'Lord, cover me with Your wings today and let me trust in Your shelter. Let Your faithful truth be my shield in every situation. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy277', 277, '2 Timothy 4:18', 'And the Lord shall deliver me from every evil work, and will preserve me unto his heavenly kingdom: to whom be glory for ever and ever. Amen.', 'Paul wrote this near the end of a hard road. He trusted the Lord to rescue him from every evil work and bring him safely home.', 'The Lord shall deliver me from every evil work and will preserve me unto His heavenly kingdom. To Him be glory for ever.', 'Lord, I trust You to deliver me from every evil work and to keep me safe all the way to Your heavenly kingdom. To You be glory for ever and ever. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy278', 278, 'Psalm 91:1-2', 'He that dwelleth in the secret place of the most High shall abide under the shadow of the Almighty. I will say of the LORD, He is my refuge and my fortress: my God; in him will I trust.', 'There is a secret place of safety in God''s presence. Dwelling close to Him, you rest under the shadow of the Almighty.', 'I dwell in the secret place of the Most High and abide under the shadow of the Almighty. The Lord is my refuge and my fortress; in Him I trust.', 'Lord, draw me into the secret place of Your presence today. Be my refuge and my fortress, and let my heart rest in Your shadow. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy279', 279, 'Psalm 91:11', 'For he shall give his angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways.', 'You are watched over more closely than you realise. God gives His angels charge to keep you in your ways.', 'God gives His angels charge over me, to keep me in all my ways.', 'Father, thank You for Your unseen care over my life. Keep me in all my ways today as I go out and as I come home. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy280', 280, 'Psalm 121:7-8', 'The LORD shall preserve thee from all evil: he shall preserve thy soul. The LORD shall preserve thy going out and thy coming in from this time forth, and even for evermore.', 'From the moment you step out to the moment you return, and for all your days, the Lord keeps watch over your life.', 'The Lord preserves me from all evil and preserves my soul. He preserves my going out and my coming in, from this time forth and forevermore.', 'Lord, I place my going out and my coming in into Your hands today. Preserve my soul and keep me in Your care, now and always. In Jesus'' name, Amen.');
INSERT INTO devotions (id, sort, reference, text, reflection, declaration, prayer) VALUES
 ('dy281', 281, 'Proverbs 18:10', 'The name of the LORD is a strong tower: the righteous runneth into it, and is safe.', 'The name of the Lord is a strong tower. When pressure rises, you can run into Him and be safe.', 'The name of the Lord is my strong tower. I run into it, and I am safe.', 'Lord, Your name is my strong tower. When trouble comes today, let me run to You first and find my safety in You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy282', 282, 'Psalm 91:5', 'Thou shalt not be afraid for the terror by night; nor for the arrow that flieth by day;', 'Whether it''s fear in the dark hours or threats in broad daylight, the one who shelters in God need not be ruled by fear.', 'I will not be afraid for the terror by night, nor for the arrow that flies by day.', 'Father, whether I face fear at night or pressure during the day, let me shelter in You. Quiet my heart and keep me from being ruled by fear. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy283', 283, 'Isaiah 54:17', 'No weapon that is formed against thee shall prosper; and every tongue that shall rise against thee in judgment thou shalt condemn. This is the heritage of the servants of the LORD, and their righteousness is of me, saith the LORD.', 'As a servant of the Lord, your heritage is His protection and His righteousness. What is formed against you will not prosper.', 'No weapon formed against me shall prosper. This is my heritage as a servant of the Lord, and my righteousness is of Him.', 'Lord, thank You that my protection and my righteousness come from You. Guard me today, and let every weapon formed against me fail. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy284', 284, '2 Thessalonians 3:3', 'But the Lord is faithful, who shall stablish you, and keep you from evil.', 'God''s faithfulness is your stability. He will establish you and keep you from evil.', 'The Lord is faithful. He will establish me and keep me from evil.', 'Faithful Lord, establish my heart today and keep me from evil. When I feel unsteady, let me lean on Your faithfulness. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy285', 285, 'Psalm 34:7', 'The angel of the LORD encampeth round about them that fear him, and delivereth them.', 'Those who honour the Lord are surrounded. His angel camps around them and delivers them.', 'The angel of the Lord encamps round about me as I fear Him, and He delivers me.', 'Lord, I honour You today. Thank You for encamping around me and delivering me. Let me rest in the knowledge that I am surrounded by Your care. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy286', 286, 'Psalm 56:3-4', 'What time I am afraid, I will trust in thee. In God I will praise his word, in God I have put my trust; I will not fear what flesh can do unto me.', 'Feeling afraid is not failure. The psalmist simply turned his fear into trust: when I am afraid, I will trust in You.', 'Whenever I am afraid, I will trust in God. I have put my trust in Him, and I will not fear what flesh can do to me.', 'Lord, when fear rises in me today, I will turn it into trust in You. I praise Your word and put my confidence in You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy287', 287, 'Psalm 31:24', 'Be of good courage, and he shall strengthen your heart, all ye that hope in the LORD.', 'Courage and hope go together. As you hope in the Lord, He strengthens your heart for what''s ahead.', 'I hope in the Lord, so I will be of good courage, and He shall strengthen my heart.', 'Lord, I put my hope in You today. Strengthen my heart and give me fresh courage for whatever lies ahead. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy288', 288, 'Daniel 3:17', 'If it be so, our God whom we serve is able to deliver us from the burning fiery furnace, and he will deliver us out of thine hand, O king.', 'Facing the furnace, three young men were sure of one thing: the God they served was able to deliver them. Your God is able too.', 'The God whom I serve is able to deliver me, and I will trust Him in the fire.', 'Father, You are able to deliver me from whatever I am facing. Give me the steady courage of those who trusted You in the furnace. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy289', 289, 'Ephesians 6:10-11', 'Finally, my brethren, be strong in the Lord, and in the power of his might. Put on the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to stand against the wiles of the devil.', 'Your strength for the battle comes from the Lord''s might, not your own. Put on His whole armour so you can stand.', 'I am strong in the Lord and in the power of His might. I put on the whole armour of God, and I am able to stand against the wiles of the devil.', 'Lord, I am not strong enough on my own, so I lean on the power of Your might. Clothe me in Your whole armour today so I can stand. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy290', 290, 'Ephesians 6:13', 'Wherefore take unto you the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to withstand in the evil day, and having done all, to stand.', 'On the hard day, the goal is simple: to stand. God''s armour makes it possible to withstand and, having done all, still be standing.', 'I take up the whole armour of God. I am able to withstand in the evil day, and having done all, I will stand.', 'Father, when the hard day comes, help me withstand. Give me grace to keep standing, even when I''ve done all I can. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy291', 291, 'Ephesians 6:14', 'Stand therefore, having your loins girt about with truth, and having on the breastplate of righteousness;', 'Truth holds you together and righteousness guards your heart. Both are given by God for you to wear today.', 'I stand, with my loins girt about with truth and with the breastplate of righteousness on my heart.', 'Lord, gird me with Your truth and cover my heart with Your righteousness. Let lies lose their power over me as I stand in You today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy292', 292, 'Ephesians 6:15-16', 'And your feet shod with the preparation of the gospel of peace; Above all, taking the shield of faith, wherewith ye shall be able to quench all the fiery darts of the wicked.', 'Walk ready with the gospel of peace, and lift the shield of faith. Faith in God quenches every fiery dart aimed at you.', 'My feet are shod with the gospel of peace. I take the shield of faith, and with it I quench all the fiery darts of the wicked.', 'Father, set my feet in Your peace and strengthen my faith. Let my trust in You quench every fiery dart of fear, doubt or accusation today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy293', 293, 'Ephesians 6:17', 'And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God:', 'Salvation protects your mind, and God''s Word is your sword. Keep a verse close today; it is a weapon the Spirit uses.', 'I take the helmet of salvation and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God.', 'Lord, guard my mind with the assurance of my salvation. Put Your Word in my heart and on my lips as the sword of the Spirit today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy294', 294, '2 Corinthians 10:4', '(For the weapons of our warfare are not carnal, but mighty through God to the pulling down of strong holds;)', 'The battles that matter most are not won with human strength. God''s weapons are mighty to pull down strongholds.', 'The weapons of my warfare are not carnal, but mighty through God to the pulling down of strongholds.', 'Father, I lay down my own weapons of worry and striving. Let Your mighty power pull down every stronghold in my life and in my mind. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy295', 295, 'James 4:7', 'Submit yourselves therefore to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you.', 'Resisting the enemy starts with surrendering to God. Draw near to Him, stand your ground, and the devil will flee.', 'I submit myself to God. I resist the devil, and he will flee from me.', 'Lord, I submit my heart and my day to You. Give me strength to resist the enemy''s lies and to stand firmly on Your side. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy296', 296, '1 John 4:4', 'Ye are of God, little children, and have overcome them: because greater is he that is in you, than he that is in the world.', 'You belong to God, and the One who lives in you is greater than anything in the world set against you.', 'I am of God, and I have overcome, because greater is He that is in me than he that is in the world.', 'Father, thank You that I belong to You. Remind me today that the One who lives in me is greater than anything I face. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy297', 297, 'Romans 8:31', 'What shall we then say to these things? If God be for us, who can be against us?', 'Think about it: if God is for you, what opposition can truly stand against you? You are not facing today alone.', 'God is for me, so who can be against me?', 'Father, thank You that You are for me and not against me. Let that truth steady my heart whenever I feel outnumbered today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy298', 298, '1 Corinthians 16:13', 'Watch ye, stand fast in the faith, quit you like men, be strong.', 'Stay alert, stand firm in the faith, and be strong. God calls you to steady, grown-up courage today.', 'I watch, I stand fast in the faith, I act with courage, and I am strong.', 'Lord, keep me watchful and steady in my faith. Give me courage and strength to stand fast today, whatever comes. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy299', 299, '2 Chronicles 15:7', 'Be ye strong therefore, and let not your hands be weak: for your work shall be rewarded.', 'Don''t let your hands grow weak. Be strong and keep going, because God sees your work and it shall be rewarded.', 'I will be strong and not let my hands be weak, for my work shall be rewarded.', 'Lord, strengthen my hands where they have grown tired. Help me keep going faithfully, trusting that You see and reward my work. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy300', 300, 'Jude 1:24', 'Now unto him that is able to keep you from falling, and to present you faultless before the presence of his glory with exceeding joy,', 'You are not holding yourself up alone. God is able to keep you from falling and to present you before Him with exceeding joy.', 'God is able to keep me from falling and to present me faultless before the presence of His glory with exceeding joy.', 'Father, thank You that You are able to keep me from falling. Hold me steady today, and let me look forward with joy to standing in Your presence. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy301', 301, '1 John 4:18', 'There is no fear in love; but perfect love casteth out fear: because fear hath torment. He that feareth is not made perfect in love.', 'Fear and God''s love can''t share the same space for long. His perfect love drives fear out.', 'There is no fear in love. God''s perfect love casts out fear from my heart.', 'Father, pour Your perfect love into my heart today. Let it drive out every fear and leave me resting securely in You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy302', 302, 'Psalm 118:6', 'The LORD is on my side; I will not fear: what can man do unto me?', 'With the Lord on your side, the opinions and threats of people lose their power over you.', 'The Lord is on my side; I will not fear. What can man do unto me?', 'Lord, thank You for being on my side. Free me from the fear of people and let me walk confidently with You today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy303', 303, '2 Chronicles 20:15', 'And he said, Hearken ye, all Judah, and ye inhabitants of Jerusalem, and thou king Jehoshaphat, Thus saith the LORD unto you, Be not afraid nor dismayed by reason of this great multitude; for the battle is not yours, but God''s.', 'When the battle looks too big, hear what God told His people: do not be afraid or dismayed. The battle is not yours, but God''s.', 'I will not be afraid nor dismayed by what is before me, for the battle is not mine, but God''s.', 'Lord, I hand this battle over to You. When it looks too big for me, let me rest in knowing it belongs to You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy304', 304, 'Exodus 14:14', 'The LORD shall fight for you, and ye shall hold your peace.', 'Sometimes standing firm means being still. The Lord fights for you, and you can quiet your heart.', 'The Lord shall fight for me, and I will hold my peace.', 'Father, thank You for fighting for me. Quiet my anxious heart and help me be still as I watch You work. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy305', 305, 'Psalm 100:4-5', 'Enter into his gates with thanksgiving, and into his courts with praise: be thankful unto him, and bless his name. For the LORD is good; his mercy is everlasting; and his truth endureth to all generations.', 'Thanksgiving is the doorway into God''s presence. Before you ask for anything today, walk in thanking Him for His goodness and mercy that never run out.', 'I enter God''s gates with thanksgiving and His courts with praise. The Lord is good, His mercy is everlasting, and His truth reaches my generation too.', 'Father, I come into Your presence today with a thankful heart. Thank You that You are good and that Your mercy never ends. Let my first words today be words of praise. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy306', 306, 'Psalm 116:12-13', 'What shall I render unto the LORD for all his benefits toward me? I will take the cup of salvation, and call upon the name of the LORD.', 'When you count God''s benefits, gratitude asks how to respond. The answer is simple: receive His salvation and keep calling on His name.', 'I cannot repay the Lord for all His benefits toward me, so I take the cup of salvation and call upon His name.', 'Lord, what can I give You for all Your benefits toward me? I receive Your salvation with a grateful heart and call upon Your name today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy307', 307, 'Psalm 147:1', 'Praise ye the LORD: for it is good to sing praises unto our God; for it is pleasant; and praise is comely.', 'Praise is not only right; it is good for us and pleasant. Singing to God lifts a heavy heart and sets the tone for the day.', 'It is good for me to sing praises to my God. Praise is pleasant, and it fits me well.', 'Father, it is good to sing praises to You. Even if my voice is tired, let a song of thanks rise from my heart today. Make praise pleasant to me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy308', 308, 'Psalm 117:1-2', 'O Praise the LORD, all ye nations: praise him, all ye people. For his merciful kindness is great toward us: and the truth of the LORD endureth for ever. Praise ye the LORD.', 'The shortest psalm carries a huge truth: God''s merciful kindness toward us is great, and His truth lasts forever.', 'I praise the Lord, for His merciful kindness toward me is great, and His truth endures forever.', 'Lord, I join all nations in praising You. Thank You that Your merciful kindness toward me is great and Your truth endures forever. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy309', 309, '1 Chronicles 29:13', 'Now therefore, our God, we thank thee, and praise thy glorious name.', 'David prayed this after seeing God''s people give willingly. Every good thing we have or do is a reason to thank Him and praise His glorious name.', 'My God, I thank You and praise Your glorious name.', 'Our God, we thank You and praise Your glorious name. Everything good in my life comes from You. Let my heart stay grateful all day long. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy310', 310, 'Psalm 34:1-3', 'I will bless the LORD at all times: his praise shall continually be in my mouth. My soul shall make her boast in the LORD: the humble shall hear thereof, and be glad. O magnify the LORD with me, and let us exalt his name together.', 'Praise is not only for good days. When you boast in the Lord, those who feel low hear it and are lifted too.', 'I will bless the Lord at all times; His praise will be in my mouth. I make my boast in Him and magnify His name with others.', 'Lord, let Your praise be continually in my mouth, whatever today brings. May my thankfulness encourage someone who is struggling. Let us magnify Your name together. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy311', 311, 'Psalm 145:8-9', 'The LORD is gracious, and full of compassion; slow to anger, and of great mercy. The LORD is good to all: and his tender mercies are over all his works.', 'God is not quick to anger or slow to forgive. He is gracious, full of compassion, and His tender mercies cover all He has made, including you.', 'The Lord is gracious and full of compassion toward me, slow to anger and of great mercy. His tender mercies are over me.', 'Lord, thank You for being gracious and full of compassion, slow to anger and rich in mercy. I rest under Your tender mercies today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy312', 312, 'Psalm 113:3', 'From the rising of the sun unto the going down of the same the LORD''s name is to be praised.', 'From sunrise to sunset, the Lord''s name is worthy of praise. Let thankfulness walk with you through every hour of this day.', 'From the rising of the sun to its going down, I will praise the name of the Lord.', 'Lord, from sunrise to sunset, Your name is worthy of praise. Help me remember You through every hour of this day and end it with thanks. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy313', 313, 'Psalm 128:2', 'For thou shalt eat the labour of thine hands: happy shalt thou be, and it shall be well with thee.', 'Honest work done in the fear of the Lord brings fruit. God sees your labour, and He can make it well with you.', 'As I walk in the Lord''s ways, I will eat the fruit of my labour. I am happy, and it shall be well with me.', 'Father, bless the work of my hands today. As I walk in Your ways, let me enjoy the fruit of my labour, and let it be well with me and my home. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy314', 314, 'Psalm 126:5-6', 'They that sow in tears shall reap in joy. He that goeth forth and weepeth, bearing precious seed, shall doubtless come again with rejoicing, bringing his sheaves with him.', 'Tears sown in faith are never wasted. God can turn a season of weeping into a season of joyful harvest.', 'What I have sown in tears, I will reap in joy. I will come again rejoicing, bringing my sheaves with me.', 'Lord, You see every seed I have sown with tears. I trust You to bring a harvest of joy from them. Turn my weeping into rejoicing in Your time. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy315', 315, 'Psalm 92:1-2', 'IT IS A GOOD THING TO GIVE THANKS UNTO THE LORD, AND TO SING PRAISES UNTO THY NAME, O MOST HIGH: To shew forth thy lovingkindness in the morning, and thy faithfulness every night,', 'Begin the day by telling of God''s loving-kindness and end it by remembering His faithfulness. Thanksgiving makes a good frame for every day.', 'It is good for me to give thanks to the Lord. I will speak of His loving-kindness in the morning and His faithfulness every night.', 'Most High God, it is good to give You thanks. This morning I declare Your loving-kindness, and tonight I will remember Your faithfulness. Let praise frame my whole day. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy316', 316, 'Deuteronomy 8:10', 'When thou hast eaten and art full, then thou shalt bless the LORD thy God for the good land which he hath given thee.', 'When you are fed and satisfied, pause and bless the Lord. Every good meal and every good place is a gift from His hand.', 'When I have eaten and am full, I will bless the Lord my God for the good things He has given me.', 'Father, thank You for food on my table and for every good gift You have given. Keep me from taking Your provision for granted. I bless Your name today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy317', 317, 'Psalm 104:27-28', 'These wait all upon thee; that thou mayest give them their meat in due season. That thou givest them they gather: thou openest thine hand, they are filled with good.', 'All creation waits on God for its food in due season. When He opens His hand, they are filled with good, and you can trust Him too.', 'I wait upon the Lord, and He gives in due season. When He opens His hand, I am filled with good.', 'Lord, I wait on You for what I need today. Thank You that You give in due season and open Your hand to fill us with good. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy318', 318, 'Psalm 111:4', 'He hath made his wonderful works to be remembered: the LORD is gracious and full of compassion.', 'God made His wonders to be remembered, not forgotten. Recalling what He has done reminds us how gracious and compassionate He is.', 'I remember the Lord''s wonderful works. He is gracious and full of compassion.', 'Lord, You made Your wonderful works to be remembered. Help me remember what You have done for me, and thank You for being gracious and full of compassion. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy319', 319, 'Psalm 103:5', 'Who satisfieth thy mouth with good things; so that thy youth is renewed like the eagle''s.', 'God satisfies us with good things and renews our strength like an eagle''s. Name a few good things He has given you lately.', 'The Lord satisfies my mouth with good things, and my youth is renewed like the eagle''s.', 'Father, thank You for satisfying me with good things. Where I feel worn out, renew my strength like the eagle''s. I receive Your goodness with thanks. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy320', 320, 'Isaiah 61:3', 'To appoint unto them that mourn in Zion, to give unto them beauty for ashes, the oil of joy for mourning, the garment of praise for the spirit of heaviness; that they might be called trees of righteousness, the planting of the LORD, that he might be glorified.', 'God meets mourning with exchange: beauty for ashes, joy for grief, praise for heaviness. He plants His people to flourish for His glory.', 'The Lord gives me beauty for ashes, the oil of joy for mourning, and the garment of praise for the spirit of heaviness.', 'Lord, I bring You my ashes, my mourning and my heaviness. Give me beauty, the oil of joy and a garment of praise. Plant me firmly for Your glory. In Jesus'' name, Amen.');
INSERT INTO devotions (id, sort, reference, text, reflection, declaration, prayer) VALUES
 ('dy321', 321, 'Psalm 150:6', 'Let every thing that hath breath praise the LORD. Praise ye the LORD.', 'If you have breath this morning, you have a reason and the ability to praise. Every breath is an invitation to worship.', 'I have breath, so I will praise the Lord. Praise ye the Lord!', 'Father, thank You for the breath in my lungs today. Let every breath I take become praise to You. Praise the Lord! In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy322', 322, 'Psalm 95:1-2', 'O come, let us sing unto the LORD: let us make a joyful noise to the rock of our salvation. Let us come before his presence with thanksgiving, and make a joyful noise unto him with psalms.', 'Worship is a joyful noise, not a performance. Come into God''s presence today with thanksgiving and a song, however simple.', 'I come before the Lord with thanksgiving. I sing to Him and make a joyful noise to the Rock of my salvation.', 'Lord, You are the Rock of my salvation. I come into Your presence with thanksgiving and a joyful song. Receive my worship today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy323', 323, 'Psalm 77:11-12', 'I will remember the works of the LORD: surely I will remember thy wonders of old. I will meditate also of all thy work, and talk of thy doings.', 'When the present feels uncertain, remember what God has already done. Recalling His past works strengthens faith for today.', 'I will remember the works of the Lord and His wonders of old. I will meditate on all He has done and talk of His doings.', 'Lord, I remember the wonders You have done in the past, in Scripture and in my own life. Let those memories strengthen my faith and fill my conversations today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy324', 324, 'Psalm 9:1-2', 'I will praise thee, O LORD, with my whole heart; I will shew forth all thy marvellous works. I will be glad and rejoice in thee: I will sing praise to thy name, O thou most High.', 'Wholehearted praise tells the story of God''s marvellous works. Share something good He has done with someone today.', 'I will praise the Lord with my whole heart and tell of His marvellous works. I will be glad and rejoice in Him.', 'O Most High, I praise You with my whole heart. Give me opportunities today to tell of Your marvellous works. I rejoice and sing praise to Your name. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy325', 325, 'Genesis 8:22', 'While the earth remaineth, seedtime and harvest, and cold and heat, and summer and winter, and day and night shall not cease.', 'Seedtime and harvest still follow each other because God keeps His promises. His faithfulness is written into the seasons themselves.', 'As long as the earth remains, seedtime and harvest will not cease. I trust the faithful God who keeps His word through every season.', 'Faithful God, thank You that seedtime and harvest, day and night, still follow Your word. Help me trust You in whatever season I am in. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy326', 326, '2 Corinthians 9:15', 'Thanks be unto God for his unspeakable gift.', 'Of all God''s gifts, Jesus Himself is the greatest, a gift too wonderful for words. Let gratitude for Him lead your day.', 'Thanks be to God for His unspeakable gift. I have received Jesus, a gift beyond words.', 'Father, thank You for Your unspeakable gift, Your Son Jesus. My words cannot fully express my gratitude, so let my life say thank You today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy327', 327, 'Psalm 16:6', 'The lines are fallen unto me in pleasant places; yea, I have a goodly heritage.', 'Take a look at the good boundaries and blessings God has placed in your life. There is more pleasantness there than a tired heart notices.', 'The lines have fallen to me in pleasant places. Yes, I have a goodly heritage.', 'Lord, thank You for the pleasant places and the good heritage You have given me. Open my eyes to see the blessings I overlook. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy328', 328, 'Hebrews 13:15', 'By him therefore let us offer the sacrifice of praise to God continually, that is, the fruit of our lips giving thanks to his name.', 'Praise can be a sacrifice when you do not feel like it. Through Jesus, even a quiet word of thanks is an offering God receives.', 'Through Jesus, I offer God a sacrifice of praise continually, the fruit of my lips giving thanks to His name.', 'Father, through Jesus I offer You the fruit of my lips today. Even when I am weary, I will give thanks to Your name. Receive my praise. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy329', 329, 'Psalm 145:3-4', 'Great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised; and his greatness is unsearchable. One generation shall praise thy works to another, and shall declare thy mighty acts.', 'God''s greatness has no end to discover. Pass on the stories of His goodness to the next generation.', 'The Lord is great and greatly to be praised. I will declare His mighty acts to the generation after me.', 'Great God, Your greatness is beyond searching out. Help me tell the next generation about Your works and mighty acts. Let my family know Your goodness. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy330', 330, 'Joel 2:26', 'And ye shall eat in plenty, and be satisfied, and praise the name of the LORD your God, that hath dealt wondrously with you: and my people shall never be ashamed.', 'After seasons of loss, God restored His people with plenty and praise. He deals wondrously with those who are His.', 'I will praise the name of the Lord my God, who has dealt wondrously with me. His people shall never be ashamed.', 'Lord my God, thank You for dealing wondrously with me. Where there has been loss, bring Your restoration. I praise Your name, for Your people shall never be ashamed. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy331', 331, 'Psalm 67:6-7', 'Then shall the earth yield her increase; and God, even our own God, shall bless us. God shall bless us; and all the ends of the earth shall fear him.', 'When God blesses His people, it is so that all the earth may come to know Him. Our blessings point others to Him.', 'God, even my own God, shall bless us. I pray His blessing on us draws all the ends of the earth to honour Him.', 'God, our own God, thank You for Your blessing and for the increase of the earth. Let Your goodness to us point many people to You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy332', 332, 'John 4:35', 'Say not ye, There are yet four months, and then cometh harvest? behold, I say unto you, Lift up your eyes, and look on the fields; for they are white already to harvest.', 'Jesus says the harvest is not someday; it is now. Look up today and notice the people around you who are ready for hope.', 'I lift up my eyes and look on the fields. The harvest is ready now, and I will share Jesus with those around me.', 'Jesus, open my eyes to the people around me who need You. Help me not to wait for a someday that never comes. Use me in Your harvest today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy333', 333, 'Psalm 40:5', 'Many, O LORD my God, are thy wonderful works which thou hast done, and thy thoughts which are to us-ward: they cannot be reckoned up in order unto thee: if I would declare and speak of them, they are more than can be numbered.', 'God''s wonderful works and thoughts toward you are too many to count. Try to name a few today and let wonder grow.', 'The Lord''s wonderful works and His thoughts toward me are more than can be numbered.', 'Lord my God, Your wonderful works and Your thoughts toward me are more than I can count. Thank You for thinking of me. Fill me with wonder today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy334', 334, 'Psalm 30:11-12', 'Thou hast turned for me my mourning into dancing: thou hast put off my sackcloth, and girded me with gladness; To the end that my glory may sing praise to thee, and not be silent. O LORD my God, I will give thanks unto thee for ever.', 'God can turn mourning into dancing and replace heaviness with gladness. Thanksgiving is the song that follows His rescue.', 'The Lord turns my mourning into dancing and girds me with gladness. I will not be silent; I will give thanks to Him forever.', 'Lord my God, thank You for turning my mourning into dancing. Clothe me with gladness today, and let my heart sing praise to You and not be silent. I will thank You forever. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy335', 335, 'Isaiah 26:12', 'LORD, thou wilt ordain peace for us: for thou also hast wrought all our works in us.', 'Peace is something God Himself ordains for His people. Whatever good has been done in you, He was the One working it.', 'The Lord ordains peace for me, for He has worked all my works in me.', 'Lord, You ordain peace for us. As this busy month begins, let Your peace settle my heart, and thank You for all You have worked in me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy336', 336, 'John 14:27', 'Peace I leave with you, my peace I give unto you: not as the world giveth, give I unto you. Let not your heart be troubled, neither let it be afraid.', 'Jesus gives a peace the world cannot give or take away. You do not have to let fear rule your heart today.', 'Jesus has given me His peace, not as the world gives. My heart will not be troubled, neither will it be afraid.', 'Jesus, thank You for leaving Your peace with me. When my heart feels troubled or afraid, remind me that Your peace is mine. Settle my heart today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy337', 337, 'Isaiah 64:4', 'For since the beginning of the world men have not heard, nor perceived by the ear, neither hath the eye seen, O God, beside thee, what he hath prepared for him that waiteth for him.', 'No eye has seen what God prepares for those who wait for Him. Waiting on Him is never a waste.', 'God prepares good things for those who wait for Him. I choose to wait on Him.', 'Father, no one has seen a God like You, who acts for those who wait for Him. Give me patience and hope as I wait on You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy338', 338, 'Isaiah 30:18', 'And therefore will the LORD wait, that he may be gracious unto you, and therefore will he be exalted, that he may have mercy upon you: for the LORD is a God of judgment: blessed are all they that wait for him.', 'While you wait for God, He is also waiting to be gracious to you. Those who wait for Him are blessed.', 'The Lord waits to be gracious to me and to show me mercy. I am blessed as I wait for Him.', 'Father, thank You that You long to be gracious to me and show me mercy. As I wait for You, fill me with the blessing of Your presence. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy339', 339, 'Micah 5:2', 'But thou, Bethlehem Ephratah, though thou be little among the thousands of Judah, yet out of thee shall he come forth unto me that is to be ruler in Israel; whose goings forth have been from of old, from everlasting.', 'God chose little Bethlehem for the birthplace of the everlasting King. Small places and small beginnings matter greatly to Him.', 'God works through small and overlooked places. The Ruler whose goings forth are from everlasting came from little Bethlehem, and He is my King.', 'Lord, thank You for choosing little Bethlehem to bring forth the eternal Ruler. Remind me that You are not limited by small beginnings. Reign in my heart today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy340', 340, 'Isaiah 7:14', 'Therefore the Lord himself shall give you a sign; Behold, a virgin shall conceive, and bear a son, and shall call his name Immanuel.', 'Centuries before Bethlehem, God promised a sign: Immanuel, God with us. His presence was always His plan.', 'The Lord gave a sign: a virgin would bear a son called Immanuel. Because of Jesus, God is with me.', 'Father, thank You for keeping Your promise and sending Immanuel. Thank You that You are God with us, and with me today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy341', 341, 'Psalm 130:5-6', 'I wait for the LORD, my soul doth wait, and in his word do I hope. My soul waiteth for the Lord more than they that watch for the morning: I say, more than they that watch for the morning.', 'Waiting for God is like a night watchman watching for dawn. The morning always comes; hold on to His word.', 'My soul waits for the Lord, and in His word I hope. I wait for Him more than watchmen wait for the morning.', 'Lord, my soul waits for You, and I put my hope in Your word. Like the watchman longs for morning, I long for You. Let Your light break through. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy342', 342, 'Micah 7:7', 'Therefore I will look unto the LORD; I will wait for the God of my salvation: my God will hear me.', 'When others disappoint and answers delay, look to the Lord. You can wait with confidence, because your God hears you.', 'I will look to the Lord and wait for the God of my salvation. My God will hear me.', 'Lord, I look to You today. I wait for You, the God of my salvation, and I trust that You hear me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy343', 343, 'Zechariah 9:9', 'Rejoice greatly, O daughter of Zion; shout, O daughter of Jerusalem: behold, thy King cometh unto thee: he is just, and having salvation; lowly, and riding upon an ass, and upon a colt the foal of an ass.', 'The promised King would come just, bringing salvation, and lowly, riding a donkey. Jesus fulfilled this, the humble King worth rejoicing over.', 'I rejoice greatly, for my King has come. He is just, He brings salvation, and He is lowly and humble.', 'Jesus, You are the King who came to us lowly and bringing salvation. I rejoice greatly in You today. Reign in my heart with Your humility and justice. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy344', 344, 'Isaiah 9:7', 'Of the increase of his government and peace there shall be no end, upon the throne of David, and upon his kingdom, to order it, and to establish it with judgment and with justice from henceforth even for ever. The zeal of the LORD of hosts will perform this.', 'The Messiah''s rule and peace will keep increasing without end. God''s zeal guarantees it, so the peace Jesus brings is not fragile.', 'The government and peace of Jesus will have no end. The zeal of the Lord of hosts will perform it.', 'Lord, thank You that the increase of Christ''s government and peace will never end. Let His peace grow in my heart and home today. Your zeal will perform it. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy345', 345, 'Luke 1:30-31', 'And the angel said unto her, Fear not, Mary: for thou hast found favour with God. And, behold, thou shalt conceive in thy womb, and bring forth a son, and shalt call his name JESUS.', 'Before the angel shared the plan, he said, Fear not. God met Mary with favour and a promise, and He meets you with grace too.', 'I will not fear, for God''s favour was shown to Mary and her Son, Jesus, is my Saviour. I receive His grace today.', 'Father, thank You for the good news given to Mary. Quiet my fears and help me welcome Jesus into every part of my life. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy346', 346, 'Luke 1:37-38', 'For with God nothing shall be impossible. And Mary said, Behold the handmaid of the Lord; be it unto me according to thy word. And the angel departed from her.', 'Mary heard that nothing is impossible with God and answered with surrender. Faith says yes to God''s word, even before seeing how.', 'With God nothing shall be impossible. Like Mary, I say: be it unto me according to Your word.', 'Lord, nothing is impossible for You. Like Mary, I yield myself to You: let it be to me according to Your word. Give me a willing heart. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy347', 347, 'Luke 1:46-48', 'And Mary said, My soul doth magnify the Lord, And my spirit hath rejoiced in God my Saviour. For he hath regarded the low estate of his handmaiden: for, behold, from henceforth all generations shall call me blessed.', 'Mary sang because God noticed her low estate. He sees you too, and His attention is a reason to rejoice.', 'My soul magnifies the Lord, and my spirit rejoices in God my Saviour. He has regarded me, even in my low estate.', 'Lord, my soul magnifies You and my spirit rejoices in You, my Saviour. Thank You for seeing me when I feel small. I rejoice in Your care. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy348', 348, 'Malachi 4:2', 'But unto you that fear my name shall the Sun of righteousness arise with healing in his wings; and ye shall go forth, and grow up as calves of the stall.', 'God promised the Sun of righteousness would rise with healing in His wings. Jesus brings light, healing, and freedom to leap with joy.', 'For those who fear God''s name, the Sun of righteousness rises with healing in His wings. I will go forth and grow in His light.', 'Lord, let the Sun of righteousness rise on me today with healing in His wings. Help me go forth and grow in Your light and joy. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy349', 349, 'Luke 1:78-79', 'Through the tender mercy of our God; whereby the dayspring from on high hath visited us, To give light to them that sit in darkness and in the shadow of death, to guide our feet into the way of peace.', 'Through God''s tender mercy, the dayspring from on high has come. Jesus shines into darkness and guides our feet into peace.', 'Through God''s tender mercy, the dayspring from on high has visited me. He gives light in darkness and guides my feet into the way of peace.', 'Father, thank You for Your tender mercy that sent Jesus, the dayspring from on high. Shine into any darkness I face, and guide my feet into the way of peace. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy350', 350, 'Isaiah 60:1-2', 'Arise, shine; for thy light is come, and the glory of the LORD is risen upon thee. For, behold, the darkness shall cover the earth, and gross darkness the people: but the LORD shall arise upon thee, and his glory shall be seen upon thee.', 'Even when darkness covers the earth, the Lord rises upon His people. Get up today; His light has come.', 'I arise and shine, for my light has come. The glory of the Lord is risen upon me, even when darkness is around.', 'Lord, thank You that Your light has come. Help me arise and shine today. Where there is darkness around me, let Your glory be seen upon me. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy351', 351, 'Galatians 4:4-5', 'But when the fulness of the time was come, God sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law, To redeem them that were under the law, that we might receive the adoption of sons.', 'Jesus came at exactly the right time, not a moment late. He came to redeem us and make us God''s own children.', 'When the fulness of time came, God sent His Son to redeem me. I have received adoption as God''s child.', 'Father, thank You for sending Your Son at just the right time. Thank You for redeeming me and making me Your child. Help me trust Your timing in my life too. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy352', 352, 'Isaiah 52:7', 'How beautiful upon the mountains are the feet of him that bringeth good tidings, that publisheth peace; that bringeth good tidings of good, that publisheth salvation; that saith unto Zion, Thy God reigneth!', 'Good news of peace and salvation is beautiful, and so are the feet that carry it. This season, you can share that good news: our God reigns.', 'I carry good tidings of peace and salvation. My God reigns.', 'Father, thank You for the good tidings of peace and salvation. Make my words and steps beautiful with Your good news this season. Our God reigns! In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy353', 353, 'Numbers 6:24-26', 'The LORD bless thee, and keep thee: The LORD make his face shine upon thee, and be gracious unto thee: The LORD lift up his countenance upon thee, and give thee peace.', 'This ancient blessing is God''s own desire for you: His keeping, His shining face, His grace and His peace.', 'The Lord blesses me and keeps me. He makes His face shine upon me, is gracious to me, and gives me peace.', 'Lord, bless me and keep me. Make Your face shine upon me and be gracious to me. Lift up Your countenance upon me and give me peace. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy354', 354, 'Malachi 3:1', 'Behold, I will send my messenger, and he shall prepare the way before me: and the LORD, whom ye seek, shall suddenly come to his temple, even the messenger of the covenant, whom ye delight in: behold, he shall come, saith the LORD of hosts.', 'God promised a messenger to prepare the way, and then the Lord Himself would come. The Lord we seek is the One who comes to us.', 'The Lord whom I seek has come, just as He promised. He is faithful to send what He has spoken.', 'Lord, thank You for keeping Your promise to send Your messenger and to come Yourself. Prepare the way in my heart for You this Christmas. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy355', 355, 'Isaiah 9:6', 'For unto us a child is born, unto us a son is given: and the government shall be upon his shoulder: and his name shall be called Wonderful, Counsellor, The mighty God, The everlasting Father, The Prince of Peace.', 'The child born in Bethlehem carries names of power: Wonderful, Counsellor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace. He is all of this for you.', 'Unto us a child is born, unto us a son is given. Jesus is my Wonderful Counsellor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father and Prince of Peace.', 'Jesus, You are Wonderful, Counsellor, the Mighty God, the Everlasting Father and the Prince of Peace. Rule over every part of my life. Thank You for coming to us. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy356', 356, 'Matthew 1:21', 'And she shall bring forth a son, and thou shalt call his name JESUS: for he shall save his people from their sins.', 'The name Jesus tells His mission: He came to save His people from their sins. Christmas is the arrival of our Saviour.', 'His name is Jesus, for He saves His people from their sins. He is my Saviour.', 'Jesus, thank You that Your very name speaks of salvation. Thank You for coming to save me from my sins. I receive Your forgiveness and freedom today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy357', 357, 'Luke 2:6-7', 'And so it was, that, while they were there, the days were accomplished that she should be delivered. And she brought forth her firstborn son, and wrapped him in swaddling clothes, and laid him in a manger; because there was no room for them in the inn.', 'The King of heaven was laid in a manger because there was no room. He still comes gently to humble places, and He welcomes you there.', 'Jesus came in humility, wrapped in swaddling clothes and laid in a manger. I make room for Him in my heart today.', 'Lord Jesus, You came humbly and were laid in a manger. Forgive me when I leave no room for You. Come and fill my heart this Christmas. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy358', 358, 'Luke 2:13-14', 'And suddenly there was with the angel a multitude of the heavenly host praising God, and saying, Glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace, good will toward men.', 'Heaven could not stay silent when Jesus was born. Join the angels today: glory to God, peace on earth, good will toward all.', 'I join the heavenly host in praising God. Glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace, good will toward men.', 'Father, I join the angels in giving You glory. Let Your peace and good will fill my home and spread through me to others this season. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy359', 359, 'Luke 2:10-11', 'And the angel said unto them, Fear not: for, behold, I bring you good tidings of great joy, which shall be to all people. For unto you is born this day in the city of David a Saviour, which is Christ the Lord.', 'Merry Christmas! The angel''s news is still good news of great joy for all people: a Saviour is born, Christ the Lord.', 'I will not fear, for I have good tidings of great joy. Unto me is born a Saviour, which is Christ the Lord.', 'Father, thank You for the good tidings of great joy on this Christmas day. Thank You for sending a Saviour, Christ the Lord. Fill my heart and home with His joy. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy360', 360, 'John 1:14', 'And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.', 'God did not love us from a distance; the Word became flesh and lived among us. In Jesus we see God''s glory, full of grace and truth.', 'The Word became flesh and dwelt among us. I behold His glory, full of grace and truth.', 'Jesus, thank You for becoming flesh and dwelling among us. Let me see Your glory, full of grace and truth, and let Your grace shape how I live. In Jesus'' name, Amen.');
INSERT INTO devotions (id, sort, reference, text, reflection, declaration, prayer) VALUES
 ('dy361', 361, 'Psalm 126:3', 'The LORD hath done great things for us; whereof we are glad.', 'Looking back on this year, name the great things the Lord has done. Gladness grows when we remember them.', 'The Lord has done great things for me this year, and I am glad.', 'Lord, You have done great things for me, and I am glad. As this year closes, help me remember each one and thank You for them. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy362', 362, 'Isaiah 46:4', 'And even to your old age I am he; and even to hoar hairs will I carry you: I have made, and I will bear; even I will carry, and will deliver you.', 'God does not carry you for a season and then set you down. From beginning to old age, He made you, bears you and delivers you.', 'The Lord who made me will carry me, even to old age. He will bear me and deliver me.', 'Father, thank You for carrying me through this year and every year before it. You made me, and You will bear me and deliver me. I rest in Your faithfulness. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy363', 363, '1 Samuel 7:12', 'Then Samuel took a stone, and set it between Mizpeh and Shen, and called the name of it Ebenezer, saying, Hitherto hath the LORD helped us.', 'Samuel set up a stone to say: hitherto the Lord has helped us. Take a moment to mark how far God has brought you this year.', 'Hitherto the Lord has helped me. Every step of this year stands as a witness to His faithful help.', 'Lord, hitherto You have helped me. Thank You for carrying me through this year. I set up my own Ebenezer of gratitude today and trust You for the road ahead. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy364', 364, 'Isaiah 42:9', 'Behold, the former things are come to pass, and new things do I declare: before they spring forth I tell you of them.', 'The former things have come to pass. God is already declaring new things, so you can face the coming year with expectation.', 'The former things have come to pass. God declares new things, and I look forward with expectation.', 'Lord, thank You for all that has come to pass this year. I open my heart to the new things You are declaring. Lead me into them with faith. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'),
 ('dy365', 365, 'Isaiah 41:13', 'For I the LORD thy God will hold thy right hand, saying unto thee, Fear not; I will help thee.', 'As you step into a new year, God holds your right hand and says, Fear not; I will help thee.', 'The Lord my God holds my right hand. I will not fear, for He will help me.', 'Lord my God, hold my right hand as I step into the new year. Thank You for saying, Fear not, I will help you. I trust You with all that lies ahead. In Jesus'' name, Amen.');
